    "notes": "20.12.17 driver with 14th Light Horse Field Ambulance, Abbassia, Egypt. 29.5.18 admitted to 65th Casualty Clearing Station with undisclosed illness. 1.6.18 admitted to 24th Stationary Hospital. 4.6.18 transferred to 4th Australian General Hospital Port Said, Egypt. 11.6.18 discharged to rest Camp. 9.7.18 injured right ankle. Inquiry undertaken to determine whether injury was self-inflicted. Soldier given benefit of doubt. Witness stated: “I was in the wagon proceeding to Jerusalem on the morning of July 8th . The brake failed to act going down a hill and the horses became unmanageable. Driver Allen jumped out of the seat and when he was seen to it was found that his ankles were sprained and jarred.” 14.7.18 rejoined unit. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Allen from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer.",
