    "notes": "20.8.15 admitted to Royal Naval Military Hospital, Malta, with septic sores to left hand and foot caused by shrapnel wounds. 14.12.15 declared fit for active duty. 26.3.16 promoted to 2nd Lieutenant at Ismailia, Egypt. 29.4.16 transferred to 57th Battalion and struck off strength of 4th Light Horse Brigade. 17.6.16 departed Alexandria, Egypt on board the Transylvania for BEF [British Expeditionary Forces] in France. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Allen from Kingston had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser published a list of all from the Borough and Shire who had been Killed in Action including Lieutenant Allen. Medals including Memorial Plaque and Memorial Scroll were sent to his mother as next of kin. 9.6.20 Trooper Allen’s mother wrote to Base Records Office, Victoria Barracks Melbourne, informing them that Trooper Allen’s father had died when William was three weeks of age and that she was now the nearest blood relative.",
