    "service": "Joined 27.10.16 Ballarat. Service number: 33498. Rank: Gunner. Roll title: FAB [Field Artillery Brigade] – Monthly Reinforcements, February to May 1917 (May to August 1917). Age on enlistment: 21 years 9 months. Occupation: Miller. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: father James Gerrerd Archibald, Smeaton. Embarked Melbourne 11.5.17 on ship A9 HMAT Shropshire. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 13/128/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
