    "notes": "13.11.16 to 20.2.17 trained as a gunner at Maribyrnong. 18.6.17 admitted to ship’s hospital A9 HMAT Shropshire with undisclosed illness. 17.7.17 disembarked Plymouth, England. 1.9.17 transferred as a Signaller to Engineer Training Depot Shefford, England. 14.12.17 embarked Folkestone, England for France. 9.9.18 treated by 37th Casualty Clearing Station, France, with PUO (pyrexia of unknown origin). 17.9.18 admitted to 3rd Western General Hospital Cardiff, Wales, with an undisclosed illness. 23.11.18 transferred to 1st Auxiliary Hospital Bulford. 1.11.18 to 15.11.18 granted furlough, upon return to report to Sutton Veny. 23.11.18 London, forfeited 7 days’ pay for being absent without permission when overstaying leave for 6 days. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Archibald from Smeaton had been a District Volunteer.",
