    "notes": "Experience prior to enlistment included New Zealand Armed Forces before coming back to Australia. 2.2.16 admitted to hospital in Ismailia, Egypt with lumbago. 10.2.16 discharged back to unit. 18.2.16 at Zeitoun Camp, Egypt, punished for losing articles from his kit due to neglect, charged for cost of items from his pay-book. 1.6.16 embarked Alexandria, Egypt, for BEF [British Expeditionary Force] France. Arrived Marseilles 8.6.16. 13.8.16 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wound to chest causing fractured vertabrae.) Transferred to 3rd Casualty Clearing Station Field, France. Died of Wounds. 19.1.17 Creswick Advertiser reported that he had been Killed in Action. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Archibald from Smeaton had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser published a list of all from the Borough and Shire who had been Killed in Action including Private Archibald.",
