    "notes": "Prior experience: membership of Smeaton Rifle Club. 20.1.15 Private Argent’s mother wrote of her consent for her son to enlist. She signed the letter with an “x” indicating that she likely had not gone to school. The letter was probably written by M. Fleisher who also witnessed the letter and signature. 2.11.15 admitted to hospital with impetigo at Gallipoli. Evacuated to Heliopolis, Egypt. 26.11.15 admitted to 1st Australian Auxiliary Hospital Heliopolis, Egypt with influenza. 1.1.16 admitted to 1st Auxiliary Hospital Cairo with septic leg. 11.2.16 discharged to unit based at Moascar Camp, Egypt. 19.3.16 embarked Alexandria, Egypt to join BEF [British Expeditionary Force] in France. 26.3.16 arrived Marseilles. 26.8.16 initially reported as Missing in Action. 20.7.17 Court of Inquiry determined that Private Argent had been Killed in Action on 26.8.16, following location of his grave.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
