    "service": "Joined Albany Western Australia 21.6.16. Service number: 6471. Rank: Private. Roll title: 16th Infantry Battalion, 18th to 22nd Reinforcements, (July to November 1916). Occupation: Railway Guard. Age on enlistment: 35 years 4 months. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at date of enlistment: Katanning Western Australia. Next of kin and address: mother, Mrs. Annie Armstrong, Rocklyn via Creswick. Embarked Freemantle 13.10.16 on ship A23 HMAT Suffolk. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original Unit 4th Infantry Battalion. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/33/4. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born 1881 Rocklyn. Birth Registration 1881/5128. Father: Thomas Henry Armstrong. Mother: Annie Robins.",
    "enlistment": "Joined Albany Western Australia 21.6.16. Service number: 6471. Rank: Private. Roll title: 16th Infantry Battalion, 18th to 22nd Reinforcements, (July to November 1916). Occupation: Railway Guard. Age on enlistment: 35 years 4 months. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at date of enlistment: Katanning Western Australia. Next of kin and address: mother, Mrs. Annie Armstrong, Rocklyn via Creswick.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Freemantle 13.10.16 on ship A23 HMAT Suffolk. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original Unit 4th Infantry Battalion. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/33/4. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "28.3.19 returned to Australia on board the ship HT City of Poona. 16.4.19 discharged 5th Military District. No Victorian death registration located.",
    "recognition": "British War Medal. Victory Medal. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W92",
    "commemoration": "",
    "warService": "",
    "nursingService": "",
    "familyConnection": "Brother, Private Wilfred Lester Gordon Armstrong [No. 3243], 11th Infantry Battalion, returned to Australia 14.5.19.",
    "additionalNotes": "18.1.19 rejoined unit in France from leave and proceeded to carry out escort duties till 5.2.19.",
    "notes": "29.12.16 admitted to Fargo Military Hospital, Birmingham England with influenza. 2.2.17 forfeited seven days’ pay for overstaying leave from Codford Camp, England. Major Twynan determined that Private Armstrong should also be held in custody for 72 hours. 12.2.17 admitted to 1st Auxiliary Hospital Bulford, England with disease. Released from hospital 19.4.17. 3.5.17 proceeded overseas to France from 4th Training Battalion Codford and embarked from Folkestone, England. 13.3.18 appointed Lance Corporal (France). 2.9.18 promoted to Corporal. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Armstrong from Rocklyn had been a District Volunteer. 17.3.19 disembarked Southampton upon return from France. Proceeded to Sutton Veny Camp on the Salisbury Plains, to await repatriation to Australia.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "Armstrong, Francis Aubrey Family Born 1881 Rocklyn. Birth Registration 1881/5128. Father: Thomas Henry Armstrong. Mother: Annie Robins. Enlistment Joined Albany Western Australia 21.6.16. Service number: 6471. Rank: Private. Roll title: 16th Infantry Battalion, 18th to 22nd Reinforcements, (July to November 1916). Occupation: Railway Guard. Age on enlistment: 35 years 4 months. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at date of enlistment: Katanning Western Australia. Next of kin and address: mother, Mrs. Annie Armstrong, Rocklyn via Creswick. Embarkation Embarked Freemantle 13.10.16 on ship A23 HMAT Suffolk. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original Unit 4th Infantry Battalion. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/33/4. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Fate 28.3.19 returned to Australia on board the ship HT City of Poona. 16.4.19 discharged 5th Military District. No Victorian death registration located. Recognition British War Medal. Victory Medal. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W92 Additional Notes 18.1.19 rejoined unit in France from leave and proceeded to carry out escort duties till 5.2.19. Family Military Connection Brother, Private Wilfred Lester Gordon Armstrong [No. 3243], 11th Infantry Battalion, returned to Australia 14.5.19. Notes 29.12.16 admitted to Fargo Military Hospital, Birmingham England with influenza. 2.2.17 forfeited seven days’ pay for overstaying leave from Codford Camp, England. Major Twynan determined that Private Armstrong should also be held in custody for 72 hours. 12.2.17 admitted to 1st Auxiliary Hospital Bulford, England with disease. Released from hospital 19.4.17. 3.5.17 proceeded overseas to France from 4th Training Battalion Codford and embarked from Folkestone, England. 13.3.18 appointed Lance Corporal (France). 2.9.18 promoted to Corporal. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Armstrong from Rocklyn had been a District Volunteer. 17.3.19 disembarked Southampton upon return from France. Proceeded to Sutton Veny Camp on the Salisbury Plains, to await repatriation to Australia.",
