    "notes": "Prior experience: Ballarat Infantry 2 years. 10.3.16 transferred to 2nd Howitzer Brigade and posted to the 104th Battery at Moascar, Egypt. 13.5.16 transferred to 4th Field Artillery Brigade. 20.10.17 dispatched to Rest Camp from 4th Field Artillery Brigade. 26.10.17 rejoined unit in the field. 24.11.17 appointed Acting Bombardier to complete establishment. 12.2.18 reverted to Driver at own request. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Driver Atkins from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer. 5.3.19 admitted to 3rd Auxiliary Hospital Dartford, England with influenza. 31.3.19 discharged to Battalion Depot Weymouth awaiting repatriation to Australia. Mentioned in Sir Douglas Haig’s Despatch of 16.3.19; London Gazette No. 31448, dated 8.7.19. 8.10.20 AIF HQ Melbourne sent an Oak Leaf to be worn with other decorations given that he had been Mentioned in Despatches.",
