    "service": "Joined 9.11.15 Ballarat. Service number: 4557. Rank: Private. Roll title: 24th Infantry Battalion, 9th to 12th Reinforcements (February to April 1916). Age on enlistment: 21 years. Occupation: Farmer (Ballarat). Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: originally his mother, Mrs. P. H. Atkins, Newlyn North. Changed to wife Mrs. Charlotte Atkins, (née Thomas) 96 Surrey Lodge, Kennington Road South London. Embarked Melbourne 21.3.16 on ship RMS Malwa. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 24th Battalion, 11th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/41/3.",
    "family": "Born Mount Prospect 13.12.1893. Birth Registration 1893/33879. Father: Henry Atkins. Mother: Phoebe Henrietta Higott. Married Charlotte Thomas 4.7.1917. Marriage Registration 1919/184 Kent UK.",
