    "additionalNotes": "5.4.19 granted approval to attend a farming techniques course at Red House Almesbury in Wiltshire. Course completed 10.7.19.",
    "notes": "17.7.16 admitted to Bulford General Hospital London with disease and discharged 3.8.16. 3.3.17 Wounded in Action France. (Shotgun wound to arm.) Embarked Calais on board the Brighton for England for further treatment. 13.3.17 admitted to Cheverley Park Hospital. 6.9.17 forfeited 5 days’ pay for being absent without permission. 11.9.17 forfeited a further 4 days’ pay on an additional charge of leave without permission. 14.10.17 departed Southampton for France to rejoin 24th Battalion. 23.7.18 Wounded in Action France. (Gassed.) Treated by 6th Australian Field Ambulance before being transferred to 47th Casualty Clearing Station. Rejoined Battalion in the field on 28.10.18. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Atkins from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer. . His mother’s maiden name was recorded as Higott on his birth registration, but Heggatt on his death registration. Next of kin was changed from his mother to his wife after he married in Wilmington, Kent, England 4.7.17.",
