    "fullProfile": "Atkins, Nathaniel Bryan Family Born Mount Prospect 13.12.1893. Birth Registration 1893/33879. Father: Henry Atkins. Mother: Phoebe Henrietta Higott. Married Charlotte Thomas 4.7.1917. Marriage Registration 1919/184 Kent UK. Enlistment Joined 9.11.15 Ballarat. Service number: 4557. Rank: Private. Roll title: 24th Infantry Battalion, 9th to 12th Reinforcements (February to April 1916). Age on enlistment: 21 years. Occupation: Farmer (Ballarat). Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: originally his mother, Mrs. P. H. Atkins, Newlyn North. Changed to wife Mrs. Charlotte Atkins, (née Thomas) 96 Surrey Lodge, Kennington Road South London. Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 21.3.16 on ship RMS Malwa. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 24th Battalion, 11th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/41/3. Additional Notes 5.4.19 granted approval to attend a farming techniques course at Red House Almesbury in Wiltshire. Course completed 10.7.19. Fate 7.10.19 returned to Australia on board ship Mahana with his wife and child. 2.1.20 Discharged 3rd Military District. Died 25.5.70 Parkville. Age at death, 77 years. Death Registration 1970/11306. Place of burial: Melbourne General Cemetery. Recognition British War Medal. Victory Medal. St. Matthew’s Anglican Church Newlyn Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E65 Family Military Connections Brother, Private Albert Victor Atkins, [No. 4734], 5th Infantry Battalion, returned to Australia 24.7.19. Cousin, Driver John Gordon Atkins, [No. 8735], 2nd Divisional Ammunition Column, returned to Australia 3.5.19. Cousin, Private Silas Atkins [No. 2952], 8th Infantry Battalion, returned to Australia 25.1.19. Cousin, Private William Henry Atkins, [No. 2034], 38th Infantry Battalion, returned to Australia 12.5.19. Notes 17.7.16 admitted to Bulford General Hospital London with disease and discharged 3.8.16. 3.3.17 Wounded in Action France. (Shotgun wound to arm.) Embarked Calais on board the Brighton for England for further treatment. 13.3.17 admitted to Cheverley Park Hospital. 6.9.17 forfeited 5 days’ pay for being absent without permission. 11.9.17 forfeited a further 4 days’ pay on an additional charge of leave without permission. 14.10.17 departed Southampton for France to rejoin 24th Battalion. 23.7.18 Wounded in Action France. (Gassed.) Treated by 6th Australian Field Ambulance before being transferred to 47th Casualty Clearing Station. Rejoined Battalion in the field on 28.10.18. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Atkins from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer. . His mother’s maiden name was recorded as Higott on his birth registration, but Heggatt on his death registration. Next of kin was changed from his mother to his wife after he married in Wilmington, Kent, England 4.7.17.",
