    "notes": "18.1.16 admitted to 2nd General Hospital, Le Havre, France with dysentery. 11.7.16 Wounded in Action France. (Shrapnel bruising to arm.) Treated by 15th Field Ambulance. Returned to duty 14.7.16. 15.11.16 admitted to field hospital with dysentery. Transferred to Le Havre for treatment. Returned to duty 14.12.16. 6.8.17 admitted to Richmond Military Hospital London with trench fever. Transferred to Australian Auxiliary Hospital on 31.8.17 and later discharged to unit on 5.9.17. 20.5.18 promoted to Corporal. 26.8.18 Transferred to Training Battalion in UK. Attended 71st course at Southern Command Bombing School Lyndhurst from 18.9.18. to 5.10.18. Qualified 2nd Class. 13.9.19 Award of Military Medal promulgated in London Gazette listed as “for bravery in the field”. Full details of citation not recorded on file. At the time of his death he was recorded as being a resident of Pyramid Hill and his occupation was recorded as retired.",
