    "service": "Joined 22.8.14 Ballarat. Service number: 269. Rank: Private. Roll title: 8th Infantry Battalion (October 1914). Age at joining, 33 years 8 months. Occupation: Labourer (Ballarat). Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: mother, Miriam Baker, Kingston. Embarked Melbourne 19.10.14 on ship A24 HMAT Benalla. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 8th Battalion, B Company. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/25/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Clunes 1880. Birth Registration 1880/23476. Father: Randall Baker. Mother: Miriam Smith Stribley.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 22.8.14 Ballarat. Service number: 269. Rank: Private. Roll title: 8th Infantry Battalion (October 1914). Age at joining, 33 years 8 months. Occupation: Labourer (Ballarat). Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: mother, Miriam Baker, Kingston.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 19.10.14 on ship A24 HMAT Benalla. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 8th Battalion, B Company. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/25/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "6.8.15 Wounded in Action while serving with 8th Infantry Battalion at Gallipoli. Subsequently Died of Wounds 20.8.15 in hospital. Age at death according to cemetery records 34 years. Place of burial: Chatby War Memorial Cemetery (Row J, Grave No. 20), Egypt.",
    "recognition": "1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. Memorial Plaque. Memorial Scroll. Kingston Fire Brigade Honour Board. Kingston State School Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W3",
    "commemoration": "Australian War Memorial, Panel Number 52, Roll of Honour.",
    "warService": "",
    "nursingService": "",
    "familyConnection": "",
    "additionalNotes": "",
    "notes": "Prior experience recorded was Maryborough Rifle Club. 6.8.15 Wounded in Action. (Shrapnel wounds to the back and left shoulder.) Admitted to 3rd Field Ambulance ANZAC then transferred to 1st Australian Clearing Hospital. Evacuated to Alexandria, Egypt on hospital ship Sicilia, but subsequently died at 19th General Hospital. 1.12.15 mother granted a Military Pension of 19 pounds per annum. Later increased to two pounds per fortnight. Some notes on soldier’s file refer to Kingston NSW but it is actually Kingston Victoria. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Baker from Kingston had been a District Volunteer. 31.1.18 Creswick Advertiser published a list of all from the Borough and Shire who had been Killed in Action including Private Baker. Australian National Archives records place of birth as Talbot.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
