    "service": "Joined 8.1.16 Melbourne. Service number: 5554. Rank: Private. Roll title: 24th Infantry Battalion, 15th Reinforcement, (July to November 1916). Age on enlistment: 21 years 8 months. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: originally to father, Albert Baker, c/o Talbot Post Office then changed to mother, Mrs. Elizabeth Baker, 243 Bellarine Street, Geelong. Embarked Melbourne 25.9.16 on ship A9 HMAT Shropshire. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 24th Battalion, 15th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/41/4. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born 10.5.1894, Parish of Talbot. Birth Registration 1894/16066. Father: Albert Edgar Baker. Mother: Elizabeth Jan Prowse. Married Dorothy Victoria May Hockaday, 1921. Marriage Registration 1921/356.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 8.1.16 Melbourne. Service number: 5554. Rank: Private. Roll title: 24th Infantry Battalion, 15th Reinforcement, (July to November 1916). Age on enlistment: 21 years 8 months. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: originally to father, Albert Baker, c/o Talbot Post Office then changed to mother, Mrs. Elizabeth Baker, 243 Bellarine Street, Geelong.",
