    "service": "Joined 5.5.16 Rockhampton Queensland. Service number: 2016. Rank: Private. Roll title: 11th Light Horse Regiment, 13th Reinforcement. Age on enlistment: 32 years 9 months. Occupation: Bookkeeper. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: John Alfred Baker, 19 Brighton Road St. Kilda, Victoria. Embarked 9.10.16 on ship A65 HMAT Clan MacEwen. Original unit: 11th Light Horse Regiment (Army Pay Corps). Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 10/16/3. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Ballarat 1883. Birth Registration 1883/13903. Father: John Alfred Baker. Mother: Martha Lynch Douglas.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 5.5.16 Rockhampton Queensland. Service number: 2016. Rank: Private. Roll title: 11th Light Horse Regiment, 13th Reinforcement. Age on enlistment: 32 years 9 months. Occupation: Bookkeeper. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: John Alfred Baker, 19 Brighton Road St. Kilda, Victoria.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked 9.10.16 on ship A65 HMAT Clan MacEwen. Original unit: 11th Light Horse Regiment (Army Pay Corps). Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 10/16/3. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "26.12.18 returned to Australia on board the ship Somali from Suez. 16.6.19 Discharged 3rd Military District as medically unfit. Medical condition not disclosed. Believed to have died 8.8.52 but no Victorian death registration located.",
    "recognition": "Twice Mentioned in Despatches. British War Medal. Victory Medal. Plaque in Western Australia Garden of Remembrance. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W4",
