    "notes": "18.10.15 originally discharged for bad conduct. Re-enlisted 6.5.16. 25.9.16, given 28 days detention for being absent without permission. 11.11.16 proceeded overseas to France with 57th Battalion. 29.11.16 admitted to 28th General Hospital Etaples, France with bronchitis. 2.12.16 evacuated from Calais for England on board hospital ship Cambria. 8.1.17 at Weymouth Camp, England, forfeited 12 days’ pay for being absent without permission on 2 occasions. 2.3.17 at Perham Downs Camp, England, given 168 hours of detention for causing a disturbance and using abusive language to Military Police. 28.6.17 Private Balfour was granted a pension of fifteen shillings per fortnight. Admitted to Melbourne Hospital, December 1917 under the direction of Master-in-Lunacy, Law Courts, Melbourne. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Balfour from Smeaton had been a District Volunteer.",
