    "service": "Joined 26.7.15 Melbourne. Rank: Private. Service number: 3526. Roll title: 6th Infantry Battalion, 10th to 12th Reinforcements, (September to November 1915). Occupation: Blacksmith. Age on enlistment: 34 years and 7 months. Marital status: Single. Religion: Methodist. Next of kin and address: originally father, W. Beasley, bootmaker, Kingston, changed to wife Mrs. F. Beasley, Queen’s Hospital, Frognal Avenue, Sidcup, Kent, England. Embarked Melbourne 11.10.15 on Ship A71 HMAT Nestor. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 6th Infantry Battalion. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/23/3.",
    "family": "Born Kingston 1881. Birth Registration 1881/3779. William Beasley. Mother: Amanda Rickard. Married Ethel May Beatrice Wilkins 6.11.17.",
