    "notes": "Unit from Nominal Roll 27th Company, Australian Army Service Corps. 21.8.15 Corporal; 23.11.16 Promoted to Wheeler Corporal; 29.9.18 Acting Wheeler Sergeant; 29.9.19 Staff Sergeant. 3.8.15 Creswick Advertiser reported that the Premier of Victoria, on behalf of the residents of the Shire, made presentations of pairs of razors (in cases) to a number of volunteers including Frederick James Beasley. 18.12.15 admitted to hospital in Heliopolis, Egypt with a poisoned finger. 1.3.16 taken on strength with 26th Australian Army Service Corps Abbassia. 8.8.16 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Beasley from Kingston was a District Volunteer. 13.12.16 based in Cairo. 16.3.19 Mentioned in Sir Douglas Haig’s Despatches. Awarded and promulgated in London Gazette No. 31448, dated 11.7.1919. On 6.7.19 admitted to hospital at sea with tonsillitis.",
