    "service": "Joined 9.3.16 Melbourne. Service number: 3925. Rank: Sapper. Roll title: Mining Corps, 2nd Tunnelling Company including No 5 Tunnelling Company (May 1916). Age on enlistment: 43 years 11 months. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: brother, Robert Boadle, Barkley Street, Footscray, Victoria. (Parents deceased.) Embarked Melbourne 25.5.16 on ship A69 HMAT Warilda. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: No. 4 Tunnelling Company, 1st Reinforcement (May 1916). Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 16/13/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Beechworth 1873. Birth Registration 1873/726. Father: John James Boadle. Mother: Kate Eustace. Married Elsie May Crocker 1920. Marriage Registration 1920/9309.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 9.3.16 Melbourne. Service number: 3925. Rank: Sapper. Roll title: Mining Corps, 2nd Tunnelling Company including No 5 Tunnelling Company (May 1916). Age on enlistment: 43 years 11 months. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: brother, Robert Boadle, Barkley Street, Footscray, Victoria. (Parents deceased.)",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 25.5.16 on ship A69 HMAT Warilda. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: No. 4 Tunnelling Company, 1st Reinforcement (May 1916). Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 16/13/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "26.9.17 returned to Australia on board the ship Borda. 24.12.17 discharged 3rd Military District as medically unfit owing to rheumatism. Died 15.11.1963 Elwood. Age at death, 90 years. Death Registration 1963/24181. Place of burial: Fawkner Memorial Park where his cremated remains were interred on 18.11.63.",
    "recognition": "British War Medal. Victory Medal. Dean State School Honour Board. Smeaton State School Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E121",
    "commemoration": "",
    "warService": "",
    "nursingService": "",
    "familyConnection": "",
    "additionalNotes": "John was officially born at Beechworth however Australian National Archives have his enlistment papers which record his birth at Smeaton.",
    "notes": "18.7.16 disembarked Plymouth, England. 26.10.16, attached to 1st Canadian Tunnelling Company. 9.2.17 returned to 2nd Australian Tunnelling Company. 12.3.17 admitted to 7th General Hospital St. Omer, France with mumps. 10.4.17 admitted to 7th General Hospital St. Omer France with osteo arthritis. 20.4.17 transferred to 4th General Hospital Etaples before being sent to London. 5.5.17 attached for duty with Training Company, AIF Headquarters Depot. 23.8.17 Medical Board determined that he was permanently unfit for general service. Sapper Boadle had informed Board that he had worked in NZ for five years but had gone to live in Queensland to relieve symptoms of rheumatism prior to enlisting. Winter 1914 in the trenches in France had severely affected his physical condition. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Sapper Boadle from Dean had been a District Volunteer. At the time of his death he was recorded as being a resident of Elwood and occupation retired engineer.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
