    "notes": "Prior experience: 4 years Senior Cadets. 15.7.15 William’s mother wrote of her approval for her son to enlist. 26.7.16 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wound to left thigh.) Transferred to England aboard hospital ship Gloucester Castle. 27.7.16 admitted to Beaufort War Hospital Bristol where he was found to be both wounded and sick. 13.10.16 Creswick Advertiser reported that he had been Wounded in Action. 13.12.16 embarked for France aboard Princess Henrietta to rejoin 8th Battalion. 14.2.17 admitted to hospital for (undisclosed) sickness. 21.7.17 Lance Corporal. 9.8.18 Wounded in Action again in France. (Gunshot wound to right foot.) Treated by 22nd General Hospital. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Boadle from Smeaton had been a District Volunteer. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
