    "nursingService": "",
    "familyConnection": "",
    "additionalNotes": "",
    "notes": "22.2.16 taken on strength with 8th Battalion Reinforcements at Serapeum, Egypt. 30.3.16 disembarked Marseilles France from Alexandria, Egypt. 22.6.16 transferred to 6th Battalion. 25.12.16 admitted to hospital in Rouen, France with trench feet. 29.12.16 embarked Rouen for London to 1st Auxiliary Hospital at Cheltenham for treatment. 31.12.16 condition was listed as severe. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Booth from Allendale had been a District Volunteer. Australian National Archives records birth at Creswick. 10.4.19 War Service gratuities passed. His war file indicates that his medical history was submitted to the War Pensions Office but there was no record of whether he was granted a pension.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "Booth, Arthur Charles Family Born Allendale 1889. Birth Registration 1889/20720. Father: Frederick Booth. Mother: Louisa Warren. Married Harriet Rose Ann Johnson 1928. Marriage Registration 1928/228. Enlistment Joined 31.7.15 Melbourne. Service number: 3249. Rank: Private. Roll title: 8th Infantry Battalion, 10th to 12th Reinforcements, (September to November 1915). Age on enlistment: 26 years. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single, Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: father, F. Booth, Allendale. Embarkation Embarked Adelaide 11.10.15 on ship A71 HMAT Nestor. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 8th Battalion, 11th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/25/4. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Fate 22.2.17 returned to Australia on board the ship Karoola. 30.5.17 discharged 3rd Military District as medically unfit with trench feet. Died 9.4.59 Heidelberg. Age at death, 69 years. Death Registration 1959/4512. Place of burial: Fawkner Memorial Park 11.4.1959. Recognition 1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. Allendale State School Honour Board. Plaque in Victorian Garden of Remembrance. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E21 War Service Egypt; France Notes 22.2.16 taken on strength with 8th Battalion Reinforcements at Serapeum, Egypt. 30.3.16 disembarked Marseilles France from Alexandria, Egypt. 22.6.16 transferred to 6th Battalion. 25.12.16 admitted to hospital in Rouen, France with trench feet. 29.12.16 embarked Rouen for London to 1st Auxiliary Hospital at Cheltenham for treatment. 31.12.16 condition was listed as severe. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Booth from Allendale had been a District Volunteer. Australian National Archives records birth at Creswick. 10.4.19 War Service gratuities passed. His war file indicates that his medical history was submitted to the War Pensions Office but there was no record of whether he was granted a pension.",
