    "notes": "Prior experience as Sergeant with Citizen Forces. 1.9.15 Quartermaster Sergeant with Light Horse Regiment at Seymour. 7.12.15 discharged as medically unfit at Ascot Vale. Rejoined 5.3.16. Promoted to Corporal 25.3.16. 5.4.16 attached for duty to 2nd Army HQ from Postal Corps. 18.10.16 taken on strength with 1st ANZAC Entrenching Battalion and promoted to Orderly Room Sergeant. 9.4.17 Promoted to Temporary Regimental Sergeant Major Warrant Officer Class 1. 6.11.17 as Corporal, taken on strength of 1st ANZAC Corps Reinforcement Camp from 1st ANZAC Entrenching Battalion. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Acting Sergeant Bourke from Allendale had been a District Volunteer. 4.12.18 admitted to 51st General Hospital Etaples, France for treatment of disease. Had three children.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "Bourke, Edward Thomas Family Born Springmount 1895. Birth Registration 1895/28544. Father: Michael Bourke. Mother: Johanna Hamilton. Married Muriel Mulbury at Talbot. Marriage Registration 1921/8386. Enlistment Joined 14.7.15 Melbourne. Service number: 3675. Rank: Acting Sergeant. Roll title: 21st Infantry Battalion, 1st to 12th Reinforcements, (June 1915 to April 1916). Age on enlistment: 19 years 11 months. Occupation: Accountant (Melbourne). Marital status: Single. Religion: Roman Catholic. Next of kin and address: father, Michael Bourke, Springmount via Creswick. Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 29.12.15 on ship A64 HMAT Demosthenes. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 21st Battalion, 8th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/38/2. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Family Military Connection Brother, Private William John Bourke, [No. 2112], 2nd pioneer Battalion, Killed in Action France 14.11.16. Fate 11.5.19 returned to Australia on board the ship Borda. 5.3.20 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 1974 Malvern. Age at death, 78 years. Death Registration 1974/8796. Place of burial: Springvale Botanical Cemetery 22.4.1974. Recognition Meritorious Service Medal. British War Medal. Victory Medal. Allendale State School Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W110 Additional Notes Awarded Meritorious Service Medal for action in the field at Etaples. Presented with Medal on 3.9.19. Meritorious Service Medal Citation: “… in recognition of valuable services rendered with the armies in France and Flanders …” Notes Prior experience as Sergeant with Citizen Forces. 1.9.15 Quartermaster Sergeant with Light Horse Regiment at Seymour. 7.12.15 discharged as medically unfit at Ascot Vale. Rejoined 5.3.16. Promoted to Corporal 25.3.16. 5.4.16 attached for duty to 2nd Army HQ from Postal Corps. 18.10.16 taken on strength with 1st ANZAC Entrenching Battalion and promoted to Orderly Room Sergeant. 9.4.17 Promoted to Temporary Regimental Sergeant Major Warrant Officer Class 1. 6.11.17 as Corporal, taken on strength of 1st ANZAC Corps Reinforcement Camp from 1st ANZAC Entrenching Battalion. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Acting Sergeant Bourke from Allendale had been a District Volunteer. 4.12.18 admitted to 51st General Hospital Etaples, France for treatment of disease. Had three children.",
