    "familyConnection": "Brother, Private Albert Gordon Boustead, [No. 55334] 1st to 17th Reinforcements, returned to Australia 6.10.19.",
    "additionalNotes": "31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser published a list of all from the Borough and Shire who had been Killed in Action including Private Boustead.",
    "notes": "1.4.16 taken on strength of 58th Battalion from 2nd Training Battalion. 17.6.16 embarked Alexandria, Egypt to join BEF [British Expeditionary Force] on board HT Transylvania. 23.6.16 arrived Marseilles France. 18.7.16 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wound to left ear.) Treated by 35th General Hospital Calais, France. 23.7.16 transferred to Convalescent Depot. 12.8.16 returned to unit. 10.10.16 admitted to 15th Australian Field Ambulance with PUO (pyrexia of unknown origin). 12.10.16 transferred to 1st Casualty Clearing Station. 13.10.16 admitted to 8th Stationary Hospital at Wimereux, France with influenza. 16.10.16 transferred to Convalescent Depot. 30.12.16 returned to unit. 13.5.17 reported Missing in Action. 13.10.17 Court of Enquiry, assembled in the field, determined that Private Boustead had been Killed in Action while serving with the 58th Battalion. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Boustead from Dean had been a District Volunteer.",
