    "service": "Joined 14.1.18 Ballarat. Service number: 69013. Rank: Private. Roll title: 1st to 17th (VIC) Reinforcements (March to November 1918). Age on enlistment: 18 years. Occupation: Baker. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: father, Mr. Thomas Boyes c/o Smeaton Post Office. Embarked Sydney 7.11.18 on ship SS Carpentaria. Ship recalled 28.11.18. Rate of pay per diem after embarkation Six Shillings. Original unit: 16th General (Victorian) Reinforcements. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/11/3. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
