    "additionalNotes": "At the time of his death, he was a resident of Glen Iris and his occupation was recorded as retired.",
    "notes": "Prior experience: 3½ years with Senior Cadets. 14.1.18 father wrote to the Recruiting Officer explaining that his son was desirous of joining and that he gave his permission for his son to enlist even though he had just turned 18 years of age. 5.2.18 Rank of Private at Broadmeadows. 28.8.18 Acting Corporal at Broadmeadows. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Boyes from Smeaton had been a District Volunteer. At the time of enlisting his mother was deceased. SS Carpentaria was recalled to Australia before reaching the war zone. As a consequence, Private Boyes was not entitled to a Victory Medal.",
