    "additionalNotes": "Her middle name is recorded as Louisa. At the time of her death she was recorded as being a resident of Ballarat and her occupation listed as spinster.",
    "notes": "Prior experience: 3 years nursing apprenticeship at Ballarat Base Hospital. 29.6.15 Ballarat Star reported that she had passed her May Exams to be a trained nurse. 11.12.17 disembarked Bombay from SS Canberra. 22.12.17 posted to Victoria War Hospital, Bombay, India. 9.5.18 transferred to staff of Welsh General Hospital, Bombay. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Nurse Brawn from Broomfield had been a District Volunteer. 10.3.19 on staff of Bangalore Station Hospital. 15.11.19 Promoted to Sister. Australian National Archives records birth at Creswick. Sister Brawn was not eligible for Victory Medal as her service did not include a war zone. Was at one time the Acting Matron at the Creswick Bush Hospital, where she already worked as a Staff Nurse.",
