    "notes": "15.10.15 Creswick Advertiser reported that she had completed 4 years of nursing at Westland Hospital (NZ); had accepted for service at the front and was awaiting her order to report for duty; departed NZ for Egypt. 27.11.15 Arrived Egypt and posted to New Zealand Hospital, Cairo. 7.3.16 serving on the Ulimaroa Hospital Transport Ship between Egypt and New Zealand. 16.6.16 serving with 27th General Hospital Abbassia, Egypt. 1.1.17 disembarked Southampton England. 19.1.17 admitted to Hospital at Sandwich (for rest). Returned to duty 25.1.17 at New Zealand General Hospital, Codford, Wiltshire. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Nurse Brawn from Broomfield had been a District Volunteer. Total service with New Zealand Defence Force 3 years 304 days. Sister Brawn was not eligible for Victory Medal as her service did not include a war zone.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "Brawn, Sister Edith Family Born Smeaton 1887. Birth Registration 1887/10340. Father: Edward Brawn. Mother: Emily Henrietta Martyr. Enlistment New Zealand Service number: 22/195. Army Record Number: 0017543. R. no: R22278571. Series: 18805. Rank: Staff Nurse. Roll title: New Zealand Army Nursing Service. Occupation: Nurse. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: sister, Mrs. Farrell, Owen River Post Office, New Zealand. Embarkation 8.10.15 embarked from New Zealand on the ship Aparima. Family Military Connection Sister, Annie Brawn, Staff Nurse, returned to Australia 8.12.19. Fate Returned to New Zealand on the Ruahine. 7.8.19 discharged from NZ forces. Died 23.12.70 at the age of 83 years, at Owen River, New Zealand. NZ Death Registration 1970/49913. Recognition British War Medal. Hollinwood State School Honour Board. Broomfield State School Honour Board. Avenue of Honour Tree W38 Nursing Service London; Egypt Her middle name is recorded as Martha. Notes 15.10.15 Creswick Advertiser reported that she had completed 4 years of nursing at Westland Hospital (NZ); had accepted for service at the front and was awaiting her order to report for duty; departed NZ for Egypt. 27.11.15 Arrived Egypt and posted to New Zealand Hospital, Cairo. 7.3.16 serving on the Ulimaroa Hospital Transport Ship between Egypt and New Zealand. 16.6.16 serving with 27th General Hospital Abbassia, Egypt. 1.1.17 disembarked Southampton England. 19.1.17 admitted to Hospital at Sandwich (for rest). Returned to duty 25.1.17 at New Zealand General Hospital, Codford, Wiltshire. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Nurse Brawn from Broomfield had been a District Volunteer. Total service with New Zealand Defence Force 3 years 304 days. Sister Brawn was not eligible for Victory Medal as her service did not include a war zone.",
