    "notes": "24.5.16 Transferred to 46th Battalion. 23.10.16, forfeited one day’s pay for being unshaven on parade. Penalty imposed by Captain Boddington of 46th Battalion. 27.2.17 admitted to hospital with septic feet. 11.3.17 rejoined unit. 26.1.18 detached for duty with 13th Field Ambulance. 14.2.18 rejoined Battalion. 9.7.18 Wounded in Action. (Gassed.) Treated by 4th Australian Field Ambulance. 19.7.18 transferred to 2nd Stationary Hospital Abbeville, France. 25.7.18 invalided to Weymouth Military Hospital England. 15.8.18 transferred to No. 1 Australian Auxiliary Hospital, Harefield, London with gas shell poisoning. 25.9.18 admitted to Bulford Military Hospital for treatment of disease. 24.11.18 discharged to Parkhouse, Sutton Veny. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Bullen from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "Bullen, Harold Family Born 16.4.1893 Newlyn. Birth Registration 1893/15237. Father: Nicholas John Bullen. Mother: Elizabeth Morrish. Married Annie Alice Frost 16.11.1921 Daylesford. Marriage Registration 1921/13066. Enlistment Joined 6.12.15 Ballarat. Service number: 4753. Rank: Private. Roll title: 14th Infantry Battalion, 13th to 23rd Reinforcements (December 1915 to November 1916). Age on enlistment: 22 years 8 months. Occupation: Farm Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Methodist. Next of kin and address: father, Nicholas Bullen, c/o Newlyn Post Office. Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 14.3.16 on ship A68 HMAT Anchises. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 14th Battalion, 15th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/31/4. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Fate 15.1.19 returned to Australia on board the ship City of Exeter. 16.4.19 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 19.12.1981 Ballarat. Age at death, 88 years. Death Registration 1981/28850. Place of burial: Ballarat General (New) Cemetery 22.12.1981. Recognition British War Medal. Victory Medal. Plaque in Victorian Garden of Remembrance. Newlyn State School Honour Board. Newlyn Methodist Church Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E75 Notes 24.5.16 Transferred to 46th Battalion. 23.10.16, forfeited one day’s pay for being unshaven on parade. Penalty imposed by Captain Boddington of 46th Battalion. 27.2.17 admitted to hospital with septic feet. 11.3.17 rejoined unit. 26.1.18 detached for duty with 13th Field Ambulance. 14.2.18 rejoined Battalion. 9.7.18 Wounded in Action. (Gassed.) Treated by 4th Australian Field Ambulance. 19.7.18 transferred to 2nd Stationary Hospital Abbeville, France. 25.7.18 invalided to Weymouth Military Hospital England. 15.8.18 transferred to No. 1 Australian Auxiliary Hospital, Harefield, London with gas shell poisoning. 25.9.18 admitted to Bulford Military Hospital for treatment of disease. 24.11.18 discharged to Parkhouse, Sutton Veny. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Bullen from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer.",
