    "notes": "Enlisted when single and gave his parents as next of kin on attestation papers. 10.10.16 admitted to Fargo Military Hospital, England with an undiagnosed illness. 19.11.16 admitted to Bulford Military Hospital and on 8.12.16 transferred to Parkhouse Military Hospital England for treatment of disease. Discharged 19.1.17. 12.2.18 admitted to Belfast Military Hospital with injury to knee (while on leave). Court of Enquiry determined that injury happened in the performance of duty (not self-inflicted). 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Caldwell from Broomfield had been a District Volunteer. Final Rank: Lance Corporal. Also known as Alex. Birth and Marriage Registration records first name as Alex not Alexander. Alexander on enlistment papers but signed as Alex. Second name David was recorded on death registration, but not listed on birth registration, enlistment papers, or cemetery records.",
