    "notes": "Prior experience included time with Rocklyn Bay Rifle Club. 27.12.17 disembarked Devonport England and immediately marched into Pioneer Training battalion Sutton Veny Camp. 7.4.18 proceeded overseas to France via Southampton. 12.6.18 admitted to 4th London Field Ambulance with illness. 14.6.18 admitted to 20th Casualty Clearing Centre with PUO (pyrexia of unknown origin). 15.6.18 admitted to 54th General Hospital. 18.7.18 transferred to Depot Convalescant Camp Le Havre France with debility. 29.7.18 returned to England. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Caligari from WA had been a District Volunteer.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "Caligari, Antonio Family Born 1875 Eganstown; Birth Registration 1875/15608; Father: Antonio Caligari. Mother: Mary Ann Lucas. Married Eleanor Jane Burford 30/1/1905 Perth, WA. Marriage Registration 1892/2709. Enlistment Joined 19.8.14 Fremantle WA. Service number: 4317. Rank: Private. Roll title: 2nd Pioneer Battalion, 12th Reinforcement. Age on enlistment: 41 years 10 months. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Roman Catholic. Address at date of enlistment: Fremantle, WA. Next of kin and address: wife, Mrs E J Caligari, 37 George Street, South Fremantle, Western Australia. Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 30.10.17 on ship A60 HMAT Aeneas. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 2nd Pioneer Battalion. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 14/14/6. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Fate 20.12.18 returned to Australia on board the ship Orontes. 28.2.19 discharged 3rd Military District as medically unfit. Died 21.7.48 Western Australia. Age at death, 73 years. Place of burial: Manjimup Cemetery. Recognition British War Medal. Victory Medal. Kangaroo Hills State School Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W103 Family Military Connection Brother: Private Baptista Patrizio Caligari, [No. 237], 4th Machine Gun Company, returned to Australia 20.12.18. Notes Prior experience included time with Rocklyn Bay Rifle Club. 27.12.17 disembarked Devonport England and immediately marched into Pioneer Training battalion Sutton Veny Camp. 7.4.18 proceeded overseas to France via Southampton. 12.6.18 admitted to 4th London Field Ambulance with illness. 14.6.18 admitted to 20th Casualty Clearing Centre with PUO (pyrexia of unknown origin). 15.6.18 admitted to 54th General Hospital. 18.7.18 transferred to Depot Convalescant Camp Le Havre France with debility. 29.7.18 returned to England. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Caligari from WA had been a District Volunteer. Additional Notes Also known as John.",
