    "notes": "25.4.17 admitted to Bulford Military Hospital for treatment of disease. 20.7.17 discharged to Training Camp. 26.10.17 proceeded overseas to France via Folkestone. 5.11.17 joined 6th Machine Gun Company in the field. 5.12.17 admitted to hospital with undisclosed illness. 8.12.17 rejoined unit. 8.8.18 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wound to face.) Treated initially by 15th Australian Field Ambulance before being transferred to 20th Casualty Clearing Station. 13.8.18 invalided to England. Admitted to Queen’s Hospital, Sidcup, Kent. 3.9.18 discharged to Littlemoor Camp. 4.11.18 granted leave until 28.1.19 from Sutton Veny to attend training course. 28.11.18 admitted to Bulford Military Hospital for treatment of disease. 4.2.19 transferred to Parkhouse to prepare for return to Australia. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Caligari from WA had been a District Volunteer.",
