    "notes": "18.7.16 disembarked Devonport and immediately taken on strength of 39th Battalion. 22.11.16 joined 3rd Pioneer Battalion in England from 39th Battalion and headed for France. 7.1.17 admitted to hospital with enteritis. 11.1.17 rejoined unit in the field. 1.7.18 admitted to 10th Australian Field Ambulance with sickness. Transferred to 5th Casualty Clearing Station. 3.7.18 admitted to 2nd Stationary Hospital Abbeville, France, with influenza. 25.8.18 transferred from France with PUO (pyrexia of unknown origin). 26.8.18 admitted to Central Midlands Military Hospital, Eastbourne, with influenza. 27.10.18 forfeited one day’s pay for being absent without permission for 6 hours. Penalty imposed by Major Simpson. 16.11.18 transferred to Overseas Training Battalion based at Sutton Veny Camp. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Cane from Kingston had been a District Volunteer.",
