    "additionalNotes": "At enlistment he recorded his birth as being in the parish of Newlyn near Ballarat.",
    "notes": "24.9.14 his mother wrote to Colonel Morton giving her permission for her son to enlist and proceed overseas on active service. 17.9.15 taken on strength of 8th Light Horse Regiment in the field. 24.9.15 died while being treated at the 16th Casualty Clearing Station. 1.12.15 Field Service Report declared that he had been Killed in Action with shrapnel wounds to his side. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Chambers from Soldiers Hill had been a District Volunteer. 30.3.20 his mother was advised that her son was now buried at Embarkation Pier Cemetery, ANZAC Gallipoli. Mother was declared ineligible for a pension as she was not dependent upon her son in the 12 months leading up to his enlistment. Regimental Number 958.",
