    "service": "Joined 1.8.17 Ballarat. Service number: 6770. Rank: Private. Roll title: 21st Infantry Battalion, 19th and 20th Reinforcements, (May to November 1917). Age on enlistment: 19 years 11 months. Occupation: Bank Clerk (Ballarat). Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: father, Robert Edward Chapman, Bank of New South Wales, Ballarat. Embarked Melbourne 21.11.17 on ship A71 HMAT Nestor. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 21st Battalion, 20th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/38/4. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
