    "service": "Joined 18.8.15 Ballarat. Service numbers: 4454 (and 4942). Rank: Private. Roll title: 8th Infantry Battalion, 13th to 23rd Reinforcements, (December 1915 to November 1916). Age on enlistment: 22 years. Occupation: Grocer’s Assistant. Marital status: Single. Religion: Methodist. Next of kin and address: father, W. Clark, Dean, Victoria. This was later changed to his wife: Grace Eliza Clark. Embarked Melbourne 7.3.16 on ship A18 HMAT Wiltshire. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 8th Battalion, 15th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/25/5. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Dean 1893. Birth Registration 1893/30918. Father: William Clark. Mother: Mary Jane Vanstone. Married Grace Eliza Summerfield 25.5.18 Registry Office Holborn London.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 18.8.15 Ballarat. Service numbers: 4454 (and 4942). Rank: Private. Roll title: 8th Infantry Battalion, 13th to 23rd Reinforcements, (December 1915 to November 1916). Age on enlistment: 22 years. Occupation: Grocer’s Assistant. Marital status: Single. Religion: Methodist. Next of kin and address: father, W. Clark, Dean, Victoria. This was later changed to his wife: Grace Eliza Clark.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 7.3.16 on ship A18 HMAT Wiltshire. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 8th Battalion, 15th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/25/5. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "12.7.19 returned to Australia aboard the ship Indarra. 9.11.19 discharged from 3rd Military District. Died 6.3.51 Ballarat. Age at death, 57 years. Death Registration 1951/16228. Place of burial: Creswick Cemetery on 8.3.1951.",
