    "notes": "24.8.16 admitted to 4th District Casualty Clearing Station Boulogne, France with a fractured patella (knee cap). 5.9.16 evacuated to England on board hospital ship Jean Breydel from Bologne. Admitted to Military Hospital Chatham. 4.11.16 discharged from rehabilitation. 9.11.16 transferred to Postal Corps for duty. 26.2.18 admitted to 1st Army District Hospital Bulford for treatment of disease. 1.6.18 admitted to St. Endell Military Hospital with infection to left knee. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Clark from Dean had been a District Volunteer. 26.5.19 admitted to 3rd Auxiliary Hospital for treatment of pleurisy. 21.6.19 discharged to AIF Headquarters. Australian National Archives records next of kin as wife, Grace Eliza. (Married before returning to Australia.) 6.9.19 Base Records advised that Private Clark, his wife and child disembarked Melbourne from ship HT Indarra.",
