    "service": "Joined 6.3.16 Perth Western Australia. Service number: 2460. Rank: Private. Roll title: 10th Light Horse Regiment, 15th to 20th Reinforcements, (April to July 1916). Age on enlistment: 30 years 10 months. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Occupation: Plumber. Next of kin and address: father, Matthew Cowan, Smeaton. Embarked Fremantle 16.5.16 on ship A52 HMAT Surada. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 10th Light Horse Regiment, 16th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 10/15/3. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
