    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 4.5.16 on ship A17 HMAT Port Lincoln. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 60th Battalion, 2nd Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/77/3.",
    "fate": "27.4.18 Killed in Action near Villers-Bretonneux while serving with 60th Infantry Battalion. Age at death, 38 years. Place of burial: Crucifix Corner Cemetery (Plot V, Row C, Grave Number 1), Villers- Bretonneux, France.",
