    "notes": "Prior experience: seven years with rifle club. 10.6.16 disembarked at Suez. 28.8.16 embarked from Alexandria, Egypt to join BEF [British Expeditionary Force]. Arrived Marseilles France on board the ship HT Franconia. 14.2.17 taken on strength 58th Battalion AIF at Etaples, France. 17.3.17 admitted to 15th Australian Field Ambulance with trench feet. Transferred to 3rd Stationary Hospital Doullens for treatment. 18.3.17 admitted to hospital in Doullens, France for treatment of disease. 12.5.17 Wounded in Action. (Shell concussion.) Admitted to 3rd Australian Field Ambulance. Transferred to Divisional Rest Station. 28.5.17 admitted to 3rd Canadian Stationary Hospital. Discharged for duty 4.7.17. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Craig from Portland had been a District Volunteer. 7.7.18 orphaned son granted a pension of 20 shillings per fortnight. Pension later increased to 25 per fortnight, then 30.",
