    "fullProfile": "Craig, Edwin Archibald Family Born Kingston 1880. Birth Registration 1880/3393. Father: Thomas Craig. Mother: Augusta Mary Smith. Married Eleanor (Ella) Mary Johnson 1911. Ella died in 1915. Enlistment Joined 11.3.16 Ballarat. Service number: 1643. Rank: Private. Roll title: 60th Infantry Battalion, 2nd to 5th Reinforcements, (May to September 1916). Age on enlistment: 36 years 1 month. Occupation: Farmer. Marital status: Widower. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: son, Archibald Albert Craig Creswick Road North Ballarat. (Young son lived with grandmother, Mrs. Margaret Johnson.) Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 4.5.16 on ship A17 HMAT Port Lincoln. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 60th Battalion, 2nd Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/77/3. Additional Notes 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser published a list of all from the Borough and Shire who had been Killed in Action including Private Craig. Fate 27.4.18 Killed in Action near Villers-Bretonneux while serving with 60th Infantry Battalion. Age at death, 38 years. Place of burial: Crucifix Corner Cemetery (Plot V, Row C, Grave Number 1), Villers- Bretonneux, France. Commemoration Australian War Memorial, Panel Number 165, Roll of Honour. Recognition British War Medal. Victory Medal. Memorial Plaque. Memorial Scroll. Kingston State School Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W26 Additional Notes Died volunteering to save a wounded man. He was shot when they came under fire while bearing the stretcher. Notes Prior experience: seven years with rifle club. 10.6.16 disembarked at Suez. 28.8.16 embarked from Alexandria, Egypt to join BEF [British Expeditionary Force]. Arrived Marseilles France on board the ship HT Franconia. 14.2.17 taken on strength 58th Battalion AIF at Etaples, France. 17.3.17 admitted to 15th Australian Field Ambulance with trench feet. Transferred to 3rd Stationary Hospital Doullens for treatment. 18.3.17 admitted to hospital in Doullens, France for treatment of disease. 12.5.17 Wounded in Action. (Shell concussion.) Admitted to 3rd Australian Field Ambulance. Transferred to Divisional Rest Station. 28.5.17 admitted to 3rd Canadian Stationary Hospital. Discharged for duty 4.7.17. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Craig from Portland had been a District Volunteer. 7.7.18 orphaned son granted a pension of 20 shillings per fortnight. Pension later increased to 25 per fortnight, then 30.",
