    "notes": "29.1.17 disembarked Plymouth, England and immediately joined the 2nd Training Battalion Durrington Camp. 3.5.17 proceeded overseas to France via Folkestone from 2nd Training Battalion Durrington camp. 5.10.17 while a member of the 5th Battalion, Wounded in Action Belgium. (Gunshot wound to left side of chest.) Treated by 64th Field Ambulance. Transferred to 11th General Hospital. 1.11.17 returned to unit. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Curran from Smeaton had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported all from the Borough and Shire who had been Wounded in Action during WW1 and that included Private Curran. 23.5.19 returned to England to prepare for repatriation to Australia. At the time of his death, he was recorded as being a resident of Smeaton and occupation pensioner.",
