    "service": "Joined 17.9.14 Ballarat. Service number: 353. Rank: Private. Roll title: 8th Light Horse Regiment (February 1915). Age on enlistment: 27 years. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at date of enlistment: Creswick. Next of kin and address: mother, Mrs. Emily Currington, Bedford Road, Great Barford, Sandy Beds, Bedfordshire, England. Embarked Melbourne 25.2.15 on ship A16 HMAT Star of Victoria. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 8th Light Horse Regiment, C Squadron. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 10/13/1.",
    "family": "Born 5.3.1887 Great Barford England. Father: Arthur Belamy Currington. Mother: Emily Buckle. Married Annie Fox 1921. Marriage Registration 1921/9524.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 17.9.14 Ballarat. Service number: 353. Rank: Private. Roll title: 8th Light Horse Regiment (February 1915). Age on enlistment: 27 years. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at date of enlistment: Creswick. Next of kin and address: mother, Mrs. Emily Currington, Bedford Road, Great Barford, Sandy Beds, Bedfordshire, England.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 25.2.15 on ship A16 HMAT Star of Victoria. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 8th Light Horse Regiment, C Squadron. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 10/13/1.",
    "fate": "23.9.19 returned to Australia aboard the HMAT Ascanius. 12.12.19 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 12.11.63 Geelong. Age at death, 76 years. Death Registration 1963/24170. Place of burial: Warncoort (Geelong) Cemetery.",
    "recognition": "Distinguished Conduct Medal. 1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E101",
