    "service": "Joined 19.4.18 Melbourne. Service number: 64571. Rank: Private. Age on enlistment: 35 years 5 months. Marital status: Married. Occupation: Farmer. Address at enlistment: Jeetho, Victoria. Next of kin and address: wife, Mrs. Margaret O. Davies, Jeetho Victoria. Embarked 14.9.18 from Sydney on ship HMAT Port Darwin.",
    "family": "Born Smeaton 4.11.1882. Birth Registration 1882/25806. Father: Evan Davies. Mother: Mary Jane Williams. Married Margaret Octavia Griffiths 4.3.1908. Marriage Registration 1908/1496.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 19.4.18 Melbourne. Service number: 64571. Rank: Private. Age on enlistment: 35 years 5 months. Marital status: Married. Occupation: Farmer. Address at enlistment: Jeetho, Victoria. Next of kin and address: wife, Mrs. Margaret O. Davies, Jeetho Victoria.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked 14.9.18 from Sydney on ship HMAT Port Darwin.",
    "fate": "25.8.19 returned to Australia aboard the ship HT Dongala. 19.9.19 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 18.5.1957 in Cobden. Age at death, 75 years. Death Registration 1056/18272. Buried at Camperdown Cemetery.",
    "recognition": "British War Medal. Smeaton State School Honour Board. Avenue of Honour Tree W30",
    "commemoration": "",
    "warService": "",
    "nursingService": "",
    "familyConnection": "",
    "additionalNotes": "Australian War Memorial advised that Trooper Davies was not taken on strength of the 15th Light Horse until 7th December 1918, after the Armistice and therefore was not entitled to the Victory Medal. At the time of enlisting, he was married with six dependent children. At the time of his death, he was recorded as being a resident of Timboon and occupation council employee.",
    "notes": "Prior experience: three years with Light Horse at Clunes. 23.9.18 admitted to hospital (at sea) with conjunctivitis. 7.10.18 Punished with 28 days field punishment for prejudicial conduct to good order and military discipline in that he left the ship against orders. 19.10.18 disembarked HMAT Port Darwin at Suez, Egypt. 30.11.18 joined 15th Light Horse at Moascar, Egypt. 24.3.19 admitted to 21st General Hospital, Alexandria, Egypt, with malaria. Australian National Archives list a number of aliases for this individual including: Gordon Richard McDonald, Rowland MacDonald, Rowland Davies, Richard Clifford Lewis. On his Death Registration, his first name was spelt Louis. Family Military Connections Brother, Private William Evan Davies [No. 1861], 4th Light Horse Regiment, returned to Australia 14.1.19. Brother, Private Phillip Edward Davies [No. 845], 3rd Light Horse Field Ambulance, returned to Australia 26.8.18.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "Davies, Lewis Rowland Family Born Smeaton 4.11.1882. Birth Registration 1882/25806. Father: Evan Davies. Mother: Mary Jane Williams. Married Margaret Octavia Griffiths 4.3.1908. Marriage Registration 1908/1496. Enlistment Joined 19.4.18 Melbourne. Service number: 64571. Rank: Private. Age on enlistment: 35 years 5 months. Marital status: Married. Occupation: Farmer. Address at enlistment: Jeetho, Victoria. Next of kin and address: wife, Mrs. Margaret O. Davies, Jeetho Victoria. Embarkation Embarked 14.9.18 from Sydney on ship HMAT Port Darwin. Additional Notes Private Davies was not included on the embarkation rolls of the Australian War Memorial. He joined the war as it was ending. He was allotted to the 15th Light Horse Regiment but wasn't taken on strength of it until 7th December 1918 after the war had concluded. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Fate 25.8.19 returned to Australia aboard the ship HT Dongala. 19.9.19 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 18.5.1957 in Cobden. Age at death, 75 years. Death Registration 1056/18272. Buried at Camperdown Cemetery. Recognition British War Medal. Smeaton State School Honour Board. Avenue of Honour Tree W30 Additional Notes Australian War Memorial advised that Trooper Davies was not taken on strength of the 15th Light Horse until 7th December 1918, after the Armistice and therefore was not entitled to the Victory Medal. At the time of enlisting, he was married with six dependent children. At the time of his death, he was recorded as being a resident of Timboon and occupation council employee. Notes Prior experience: three years with Light Horse at Clunes. 23.9.18 admitted to hospital (at sea) with conjunctivitis. 7.10.18 Punished with 28 days field punishment for prejudicial conduct to good order and military discipline in that he left the ship against orders. 19.10.18 disembarked HMAT Port Darwin at Suez, Egypt. 30.11.18 joined 15th Light Horse at Moascar, Egypt. 24.3.19 admitted to 21st General Hospital, Alexandria, Egypt, with malaria. Australian National Archives list a number of aliases for this individual including: Gordon Richard McDonald, Rowland MacDonald, Rowland Davies, Richard Clifford Lewis. On his Death Registration, his first name was spelt Louis. Family Military Connections Brother, Private William Evan Davies [No. 1861], 4th Light Horse Regiment, returned to Australia 14.1.19. Brother, Private Phillip Edward Davies [No. 845], 3rd Light Horse Field Ambulance, returned to Australia 26.8.18.",
