    "notes": "25.10.15 admitted to 4th Auxiliary Hospital Abbassia, Egypt with diphtheria. 8.11.15 discharged to unit. 31.3.16 reported to 3rd Light Horse Field Ambulance with influenza. Transferred to 2nd Australian Casualty Clearing Station. 1.4.16 discharged to unit. 16.4.16 readmitted to Hospital. 21.4.16 rejoined unit at Serapaum. 4.10.16 admitted to 26th Casualty Clearing Station with malaria. 12.10.16 admitted to 31st General Hospital Port Said, Egypt with malaria and debility. Transferred to Cairo on Hospital Train. 22.2.17 discharged to unit. 4.4.17 forfeited 2 days’ pay for smoking on parade. 17.7.17 forfeited 6 shillings per day for 4 days for shouting out after lights out. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Driver Davies from “Merrifield” (near Clunes) had been a District Volunteer. Family Military Connections Brother, Private Lewis Rowland Davies, [No. 64571], 15th Light Horse Regiment, returned to Australia 25.8.19. Brother, Private William Evan Davies, [No. 1861], 4th Light Horse Regiment, returned to Australia 14.1.19.",
