    "notes": "18.11.15 disembarked Suez. 8.1.16 joined Auckland Infantry Battalion at Moascar Camp, Egypt. 6.4.16 embarked Port Said, Egypt aboard Franconia for France. 31.10.16 attached to NZ Engineers. 12.3.17 as part of 1st Auckland Regiment was responsible for assisting engineers in laying communication cables in the vicinity of Rouen, France. 11.6.17 Reported as Wounded in Action. (Nature of wounding not specified.) 8.7.17 reported as Wounded and Missing in Action. Court of Inquiry held 13.8.1917 found that he had been Killed in Action c. 7.6.1917. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Godfrey from Clementston had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser published a list of all from the Borough and Shire who had been Killed in Action including Private Godfrey.",
