    "fullProfile": "Godfrey, Herbert Family Born Ararat 6.2.1890. Birth Registration 1890/27. Father: Thomas Alfred Godfrey. Mother: Elizabeth Matthews. Enlistment Joined 11.6.15 New Zealand. Service number: 12/3026. NZ Army number: 0045440 R16. Rank: Private. Age on enlistment: 26 years. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at date of enlistment: Oranga NZ. Next of kin and address: father, Mr. T. A. Godfrey, cnr. Tuson and Temple Streets, Ararat. Embarkation Embarked 9.10.15 from Wellington New Zealand. Original unit: Auckland Infantry Battalion, 7th reinforcements. (Ship details are unclear as three different vessels are recorded.) Family Military Connection Brother, Sergeant Cecil Edwin Godfrey, [No. 8606], 6th Field Artillery Brigade, returned to Australia 10.6.19. Fate 7.6.17 Killed in Action, Belgium. No Known Grave. Commemoration Belgium, Messines Ridge NZ Memorial, Mosen, West- Vlaanderen [West Flanders], Belgium. Remembrance Auckland War Memorial Museum, WW1 Hall of Memories. Recognition 1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. Memorial Plaque. Memorial Scroll. Avenue of Honour Tree E135 Additional Notes Medals together with Memorial Scroll and Memorial Plaque were forwarded to his father (as next of kin) in Ararat. Notes 18.11.15 disembarked Suez. 8.1.16 joined Auckland Infantry Battalion at Moascar Camp, Egypt. 6.4.16 embarked Port Said, Egypt aboard Franconia for France. 31.10.16 attached to NZ Engineers. 12.3.17 as part of 1st Auckland Regiment was responsible for assisting engineers in laying communication cables in the vicinity of Rouen, France. 11.6.17 Reported as Wounded in Action. (Nature of wounding not specified.) 8.7.17 reported as Wounded and Missing in Action. Court of Inquiry held 13.8.1917 found that he had been Killed in Action c. 7.6.1917. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Godfrey from Clementston had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser published a list of all from the Borough and Shire who had been Killed in Action including Private Godfrey.",
