    "id": 103,
    "treeNum": "E144",
    "name": "Gore, Reginald Malpas",
    "gender": "Male",
    "rank": "Private",
    "role": "Soldier",
    "location": "Kingston",
    "service": "Joined 2.9.14 Gympie, Queensland. Service number: 260. Rank: Private. Roll title: 9th Infantry Battalion (September 1914). Age on enlistment: 19 years 5 months. Occupation: Grocer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at date of enlistment: Glenrowan, Murgon, Queensland. Next of kin and address: father, Alfred Joseph Gore, 2 Cherry Garden Avenue, Folkestone England. Embarked Brisbane 24.9.14 on ship A5 HMAT Omrah. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 9th Battalion, B Company. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/26/1. Family Military Connections His brothers, Sydney Kingston Gore and Cecil Gore, enlisted with the British Army in World War 1. Sydney Kingston Gore died in battle in 1914. Cecil Gore transferred to the Indian Army after World War 1.",
    "family": "Born 22.4.1895, Chester, Cheshire, England. Father: Alfred Joseph Gore. Married Helen Elizabeth Mary Mayne 1923 in Kodaikanal, South India.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 2.9.14 Gympie, Queensland. Service number: 260. Rank: Private. Roll title: 9th Infantry Battalion (September 1914). Age on enlistment: 19 years 5 months. Occupation: Grocer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at date of enlistment: Glenrowan, Murgon, Queensland. Next of kin and address: father, Alfred Joseph Gore, 2 Cherry Garden Avenue, Folkestone England.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Brisbane 24.9.14 on ship A5 HMAT Omrah. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 9th Battalion, B Company. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/26/1. Family Military Connections His brothers, Sydney Kingston Gore and Cecil Gore, enlisted with the British Army in World War 1. Sydney Kingston Gore died in battle in 1914. Cecil Gore transferred to the Indian Army after World War 1.",
    "fate": "2.5.18 discharged in England following the grant of a commission with Indian Army. Died 19.4.1969, Hartismere, Suffolk, England.",
    "recognition": "King’s Police Medal for Gallantry. 1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. General Service Medal. 1939–45 Star. Burma Star. War Medal 1939–45. Indian Service Medal 1939–45. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E144",
    "commemoration": "",
    "warService": "Gallipoli; Egypt; Western Front.",
    "nursingService": "",
    "familyConnection": "",
    "additionalNotes": "Stayed in Britain after WW1, where he served with the 1st Battalion in India between 1920-1923. Served with the Indian Army through World War 2 and retired on Indian independence in 1947. Returned to Australia and worked with the National Bank at Warrnambool.",
    "notes": "Corporal from 12.8.15; Sergeant from 1.3.16 at Tel- el-Kebir, Egypt; 2nd Lieutenant from 5.4.16 at Serapeum, Egypt; Captain from 26.7.17. 25.2.16 joined 49th Battalion. 25.11.16 admitted to hospital with undisclosed illness. Admitted to 39th General Hospital Le Havre, France. Also diagnosed with trench catarrh. Transferred to 8th General Hospital for treatment of disease. 4.8.17 detached to 13th Training Battalion, England. 28.9.17 as Captain, attended and qualified at the School of Musketry, Tidworth Camp. 26.11.17 attended and qualified as First Class at the 5th Lewis Machine Gun Course at the School of Musketry, Tidworth camp. 2.5.18 commissioned in the Indian Army. Worked in Kingston. His grandfather was Henry Gore of Kingston. Enlisted while visiting relatives in Queensland.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "Gore, Reginald Malpas Family Born 22.4.1895, Chester, Cheshire, England. Father: Alfred Joseph Gore. Married Helen Elizabeth Mary Mayne 1923 in Kodaikanal, South India. Enlistment Joined 2.9.14 Gympie, Queensland. Service number: 260. Rank: Private. Roll title: 9th Infantry Battalion (September 1914). Age on enlistment: 19 years 5 months. Occupation: Grocer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at date of enlistment: Glenrowan, Murgon, Queensland. Next of kin and address: father, Alfred Joseph Gore, 2 Cherry Garden Avenue, Folkestone England. Embarkation Embarked Brisbane 24.9.14 on ship A5 HMAT Omrah. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 9th Battalion, B Company. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/26/1. Family Military Connections His brothers, Sydney Kingston Gore and Cecil Gore, enlisted with the British Army in World War 1. Sydney Kingston Gore died in battle in 1914. Cecil Gore transferred to the Indian Army after World War 1. Fate 2.5.18 discharged in England following the grant of a commission with Indian Army. Died 19.4.1969, Hartismere, Suffolk, England. Recognition King’s Police Medal for Gallantry. 1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. General Service Medal. 1939–45 Star. Burma Star. War Medal 1939–45. Indian Service Medal 1939–45. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E144 Additional Notes Stayed in Britain after WW1, where he served with the 1st Battalion in India between 1920-1923. Served with the Indian Army through World War 2 and retired on Indian independence in 1947. Returned to Australia and worked with the National Bank at Warrnambool. Notes Corporal from 12.8.15; Sergeant from 1.3.16 at Tel- el-Kebir, Egypt; 2nd Lieutenant from 5.4.16 at Serapeum, Egypt; Captain from 26.7.17. 25.2.16 joined 49th Battalion. 25.11.16 admitted to hospital with undisclosed illness. Admitted to 39th General Hospital Le Havre, France. Also diagnosed with trench catarrh. Transferred to 8th General Hospital for treatment of disease. 4.8.17 detached to 13th Training Battalion, England. 28.9.17 as Captain, attended and qualified at the School of Musketry, Tidworth Camp. 26.11.17 attended and qualified as First Class at the 5th Lewis Machine Gun Course at the School of Musketry, Tidworth camp. 2.5.18 commissioned in the Indian Army. Worked in Kingston. His grandfather was Henry Gore of Kingston. Enlisted while visiting relatives in Queensland. War Service Gallipoli; Egypt; Western Front.",
