    "nursingService": "",
    "familyConnection": "",
    "additionalNotes": "Birth recorded as Albert Green, death recorded as Albert John Green. Death registration records his age as 82.",
    "notes": "2.6.16 departed Alexandria, Egypt to join BEF [British Expeditionary Force] in France. 8.6.16 disembarked Marseilles. 2.9.16 treated for diphtheria, rejoined unit 9.9.16. 4.10.17 recommended for Military Medal. 22.5.1918 awarded Military Medal. 18.9.18 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wound to right arm.) Admitted to Royal Victoria Hospital, Netley, Southampton, Hampshire. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Green from Springmount had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported on all from the Borough and Shire who had been Wounded in Action during WW1 and that included Driver Green. 16.3.19 returned to Australia with fractured right humerus (upper arm). Military Medal Citation: “On the night 30th September, 1917, near WESTHOEK Driver GREEN showed great coolness under heavy shell fire. The limber and one of the mules was hit by a shell, the mule being wounded about the head. The harness was badly broken by pieces of shell. He pulled up the team, repaired the harness temporarily despite the heavy shelling and by remaining with his team pacified the frightened animals and saved the limber [cart] and team of four.”",
