    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 18.4.16 on ship A53 HMAT Itria. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 4th Light Horse Regiment, 16th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 10/9/3. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "22.12.18 returned to Australia on board the ship HT Leicestershire. 12.6.19 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 2.8.1931 Dean. Age at death, 42 years. Death Registration 1931/9031. Place of burial: Creswick Cemetery on 4.8.1931 where he was recorded as a resident of Newlyn.",
    "recognition": "British War Medal. Victory Medal. Newlyn State School Honour Board. Scrub Hill Uniting Church Newlyn Honour Board. Newlyn Methodist Church Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E41",
    "commemoration": "",
    "warService": "",
    "nursingService": "",
    "familyConnection": "",
    "additionalNotes": "3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Grigg from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer.",
    "notes": "Prior experience: three years with 19th Light Horse Regiment and one year as a senior cadet. 31.1.16 joined AIF Signal School Broadmeadows. 2.11.16 joined Camel Corps at El Erdau (Alexandria) Egypt. 25.2.17 joined 4th Light Horse Regiment from Camel Training Unit. 19.5.17 Detached to Hotchkiss Gun School Zeitoun, Egypt. 29.5.17 taken on strength of 1st Light Horse Training Regiment. 6.7.17 taken on strength of Double Squadron. 9.8.17 taken on strength of 1st Light Horse at Tel-el-Kebir. 4.7.18 admitted to 14th General Hospital AIF with malaria. 14.9.18 considered to be dangerously ill with malaria in Port Said, Egypt. 23.10.18 reported to be convalescing. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported all from the Borough and Shire who had been Wounded in Action during WW1 and that included Private Grigg. Private Grigg died due to the malaria he had contracted during the war.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "Grigg, William John Family Born Newlyn 1889. Birth Registration 1895/2805. Father: Richard Hobbs Grigg. Mother: Mary Warner. Married Florence May Moore 1922. Marriage Registration 1922/2346. Enlistment Joined 15.1.16 Ballarat. Service number: 2333. Rank: Private. Roll title: 4th Light Horse Regiment, 13th to 25th Reinforcements (January 1916 to January 1917). Age on enlistment: 21 years 1 month. Occupation: Farmer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Methodist. Next of kin and address: father, Richard Hobbs Grigg, Newlyn. Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 18.4.16 on ship A53 HMAT Itria. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 4th Light Horse Regiment, 16th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 10/9/3. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Additional Notes At the time of his death, he was recorded as being a resident of Newlyn and occupation farmer. Fate 22.12.18 returned to Australia on board the ship HT Leicestershire. 12.6.19 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 2.8.1931 Dean. Age at death, 42 years. Death Registration 1931/9031. Place of burial: Creswick Cemetery on 4.8.1931 where he was recorded as a resident of Newlyn. Recognition British War Medal. Victory Medal. Newlyn State School Honour Board. Scrub Hill Uniting Church Newlyn Honour Board. Newlyn Methodist Church Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E41 Additional Notes 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Grigg from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer. Notes Prior experience: three years with 19th Light Horse Regiment and one year as a senior cadet. 31.1.16 joined AIF Signal School Broadmeadows. 2.11.16 joined Camel Corps at El Erdau (Alexandria) Egypt. 25.2.17 joined 4th Light Horse Regiment from Camel Training Unit. 19.5.17 Detached to Hotchkiss Gun School Zeitoun, Egypt. 29.5.17 taken on strength of 1st Light Horse Training Regiment. 6.7.17 taken on strength of Double Squadron. 9.8.17 taken on strength of 1st Light Horse at Tel-el-Kebir. 4.7.18 admitted to 14th General Hospital AIF with malaria. 14.9.18 considered to be dangerously ill with malaria in Port Said, Egypt. 23.10.18 reported to be convalescing. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported all from the Borough and Shire who had been Wounded in Action during WW1 and that included Private Grigg. Private Grigg died due to the malaria he had contracted during the war.",
