    "service": "Joined 27.1.15 Ballarat. Service number: 163. Rank: Private. Roll title: 22nd Infantry Battalion (May 1915). Age on enlistment: 18 years 3 months. Occupation: Farmer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: step-sister, A. Allan, c/o W. Smith Camberwell, also father (and mother), T. Grisby, 37 Nicholson Street Ballarat East. Embarked Melbourne 10.5.15 on ship A38 HMAT Ulysses. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 22nd Battalion, A Company. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/39/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Ballarat 1899. Birth Registration 1899/356. Father: Thomas Grigsby. Mother: Minnie Allen.",
