    "notes": "30.8.15 proceeded to join MEF [Mediterranean Expeditionary Force] at Gallipoli. 19.3.16 departed Alexandria, Egypt to join MEF in France. 26.3.16 disembarked Marseilles. 5.8.16 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wound to left leg.) Admitted to 8th General Hospital. Embarked Le Havre, France for England aboard hospital ship HS Mahena. 10.8.16 admitted to Beaufort War Hospital, Fishponds, Bristol. 12.11.16 discharged from 3rd Auxiliary Hospital Weymouth. 13.10.16 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Grigsby had been Wounded in Action. 4.5.17 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wound to head.) Treated by 3rd Casualty Clearing Station. Admitted to 9th General Hospital Rouen, France. 23.5.17 discharged to Base Depot. 2.6.17 rejoined Battalion. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Grigsby from Dean had been a District Volunteer. National Archives records next of kin as mother, T. Grigsby.",
