    "location": "Creswick / Allendale",
    "service": "Joined 19.05.16 Kalgoorlie, Western Australia. Service number: 2681A. Rank: Private. Roll title: 16th Infantry Battalion, 22nd Reinforcements. Age on enlistment: 32 years 10 months. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Roman Catholic. Next of kin and address: Sister, Maggi Walsh, Elizabeth Street, Allendale. (Not on Embarkation Roll.) Embarked Fremantle 30.10.16 on ship A16 HMAT Port Melbourne. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 16th Battalion, 22nd Reinforcement.",
    "family": "Born Allendale, Vic 1883. Birth Registration 20903/1883. Father: Patrick Hanley. Mother: Mary Gallagher. Married Aileen Margaret Harrington 27.12.1923. Marriage Registration 10988/1923.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 19.05.16 Kalgoorlie, Western Australia. Service number: 2681A. Rank: Private. Roll title: 16th Infantry Battalion, 22nd Reinforcements. Age on enlistment: 32 years 10 months. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Roman Catholic. Next of kin and address: Sister, Maggi Walsh, Elizabeth Street, Allendale.",
    "embarkation": "(Not on Embarkation Roll.) Embarked Fremantle 30.10.16 on ship A16 HMAT Port Melbourne. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 16th Battalion, 22nd Reinforcement.",
    "fate": "3.3.19 returned to Australia aboard H.T Euripides. 2.6.19 discharged 3rd Military District. Discharge due to Termination of Period of Enlistment [TPE]. Died 1.12.1976 Macleod Repatriation Hospital. Age at death, 94 years. Death Registration 1976/29576. Place of burial: Boroondara General Cemetery (Kew).",
    "recognition": "British War Medal. Victory Medal. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Allendale State School Honor Board. Avenue of Honour Tree W128",
    "commemoration": "",
    "warService": "",
    "nursingService": "",
    "familyConnection": "",
    "additionalNotes": "11.5.17 The Ballarat Courier initially reported him missing, stating that his family had resided at Allendale for many years before moving away. He was well-known in football circles, having played with the local club before joining the Golden Point Club and the Essendon Leagues team.",
    "notes": "24.11.16 He was made Lance Corporal for Voyage only. 10.2.17 transferred On Strength to main group of 48th Battalion from 6th Reinforcements of 48th Battalion. 11.4.17 Reported Missing in Action in the field. Later reported captured as a Prisoner of War, interred at Limburg, Germany. 15.9.17 Re-interred at Dulmen Camp 46A, Barrack III, Detainee 39341. 22.9.17 Ballarat Courier reported as Prisoner of War in Germany. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Hanley from Western Australia had been a District Volunteer. 30.12.18 Prisoner was repatriated back to England. 7.2.19 Mistakenly fined for being AWOL when instead was reporting to Headquarters. 12.2.19 Marched into No.1 Command Depot at Sutton Veny for return to Australia.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "Hanley, Daniel Family Born Allendale, Vic 1883. Birth Registration 20903/1883. Father: Patrick Hanley. Mother: Mary Gallagher. Married Aileen Margaret Harrington 27.12.1923. Marriage Registration 10988/1923. Enlistment Joined 19.05.16 Kalgoorlie, Western Australia. Service number: 2681A. Rank: Private. Roll title: 16th Infantry Battalion, 22nd Reinforcements. Age on enlistment: 32 years 10 months. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Roman Catholic. Next of kin and address: Sister, Maggi Walsh, Elizabeth Street, Allendale. Embarkation (Not on Embarkation Roll.) Embarked Fremantle 30.10.16 on ship A16 HMAT Port Melbourne. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 16th Battalion, 22nd Reinforcement. Additional Notes At the time of his death, he was recorded as being a resident of Phillipson Street, Albert Park. Also known as Dan. Fate 3.3.19 returned to Australia aboard H.T Euripides. 2.6.19 discharged 3rd Military District. Discharge due to Termination of Period of Enlistment [TPE]. Died 1.12.1976 Macleod Repatriation Hospital. Age at death, 94 years. Death Registration 1976/29576. Place of burial: Boroondara General Cemetery (Kew). Recognition British War Medal. Victory Medal. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Allendale State School Honor Board. Avenue of Honour Tree W128 Additional Notes 11.5.17 The Ballarat Courier initially reported him missing, stating that his family had resided at Allendale for many years before moving away. He was well-known in football circles, having played with the local club before joining the Golden Point Club and the Essendon Leagues team. Notes 24.11.16 He was made Lance Corporal for Voyage only. 10.2.17 transferred On Strength to main group of 48th Battalion from 6th Reinforcements of 48th Battalion. 11.4.17 Reported Missing in Action in the field. Later reported captured as a Prisoner of War, interred at Limburg, Germany. 15.9.17 Re-interred at Dulmen Camp 46A, Barrack III, Detainee 39341. 22.9.17 Ballarat Courier reported as Prisoner of War in Germany. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Hanley from Western Australia had been a District Volunteer. 30.12.18 Prisoner was repatriated back to England. 7.2.19 Mistakenly fined for being AWOL when instead was reporting to Headquarters. 12.2.19 Marched into No.1 Command Depot at Sutton Veny for return to Australia.",
