    "service": "Joined 13.7.15 Melbourne. Service number: 3156. Rank: Private. Roll title: 14th Infantry Battalion, 5th to 12th Reinforcements, (April to November 1915). Age on enlistment: 25 years 9 months. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: grandmother, Mrs. Elizabeth Kelso, Smeaton. (Both parents deceased.) Embarked Melbourne 16.10.15 on ship A17 HMAT Port Lincoln. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 14th Battalion, 10th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/31/3. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Smeaton 1890. Birth Registration 1890/36521. Father: John Matthew Harris. Mother: Jane Kelso.",
