    "notes": "4.2.16 taken on strength with 14th Battalion at Moascar Camp, Egypt. 25.1.17 Medical Board Report recommended discharge as permanently unfit. 6.2.17 transferred from Reading War Hospital to 1st Auxiliary Hospital suffering from bronchitis. 6.4.17 Private Harris’s grandmother (as next of kin) was granted a pension of fifteen shillings per fortnight. 10.4.17 Admitted to Reading War Hospital with bronchitis. Found to be suffering from tuberculosis. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Harris from Smeaton had been a District Volunteer. 5.10.23 medals were sent to his grandmother Mrs. Elizabeth Kelso in Smeaton. Private Harris died in Australia from a war illness and was entitled to be commemorated at the Australian War Memorial because he died within 12 months of the war ending.",
