    "notes": "Prior experience: 12 months with Senior Cadets but exempted from Citizen Forces on account of his height. 22.11.15 transferred to Signal School AIF Broadmeadows from Light Horse at Seymour. 11.3.16 taken on strength of 14th Battalion AIF at Tel-el- Kebir, Egypt. 1.6.16 departed Alexandria, Egypt, to join the BEF [British Expeditionary Force] in France. 8.6.16 disembarked at Marseilles France. 1.10.17 promoted to Lance Corporal. 29.2.18 promoted to Corporal. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Heron from Newport had been a District Volunteer. 31.1.24 AIF Base Records Office sent three photographs of the temporary Cross erected in Private Heron’s memory pending the design and laying of a permanent headstone. Family Military Connections Cousin, Private Duncan Heron, [No. 392], 21st Infantry, returned to Australia 21.4.18. Brother, Corporal Walter Francis Heron [No. 1185], 15th Infantry Battalion, returned to Australia 1.11.18.",
