    "service": "Joined 17.9.14 Pontville, Tasmania. Service number: 1185. Rank: Corporal. Roll title: 15th Infantry Battalion (December 1914). Age on enlistment: 21 years. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Occupation: Labourer, (Pontville Tasmania). Next of kin and address: father, J. Heron, 2 Waltham Road, Newport. Embarked Melbourne 22.12.14 on ship A40 HMAT Ceramic. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 15th Battalion, H Company. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/32/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Springmount 1893. Birth Registration 1893/114. Father: John Heron. Mother: Jane Gostellow. Married Mirron Ann Elizabeth Norris 1922. Marriage Registration 1922/8979.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 17.9.14 Pontville, Tasmania. Service number: 1185. Rank: Corporal. Roll title: 15th Infantry Battalion (December 1914). Age on enlistment: 21 years. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Occupation: Labourer, (Pontville Tasmania). Next of kin and address: father, J. Heron, 2 Waltham Road, Newport.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 22.12.14 on ship A40 HMAT Ceramic. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 15th Battalion, H Company. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/32/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "1.11.18 returned to Australia on board the ship HT Port Lyttleton. 20.3.19 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 1.11.1974 Parkville. Age at death, 81 years. Death Registration 1974/28953. Cremated at Fawkner Memorial Park 6.11.74.",
