    "family": "Born Kingston 22.5.1892. Birth Registration 1892/14857. Father: Robert Hodgson. Mother: Margaret Wilson. Married Muriel Doris McDowell 1919. Marriage Registration 1919/9086.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 14.8.14. Rank: Lieutenant. Roll title: 2nd FAB [Field Artillery Brigade], (October 1914). Age on enlistment: 22 years 4 months. Marital status: Single. Occupation: Soldier. Next of kin and address: Mrs. R. Hodgson, Colac.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 20.10.14 on ship A9 HMAT Shropshire. Rate of pay per diem before embarkation: Fifteen Shillings. Rate of pay per diem after embarkation: Fourteen Shillings Six Pence. Original unit: Field Artillery 2nd Brigade 5th Battery, 1st Division Artillery. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 13/30/1.",
    "fate": "22.2.17 returned to Australia on board the ship Karola. 2.7.17 discharged 3rd Military District as medically unfit. Died 1978. Age at death, 86 years. Cremated at Altona Memorial Park.",
