    "service": "Joined 15.9.14 Kingston. Service number: 208. Rank: Private. Roll title: 14th Infantry Battalion (December 1914). Age on enlistment: 37 years. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Married. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: wife, Mrs. L. L. Hopkins, Allendale. Embarked Melbourne 22.12.14 on ship A38 HMAT Ulysses. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 14th Battalion, B Company. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/31/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Maryborough 1874. Birth Registration 1874/10061. Father: John Hopkins. Mother: Elizabeth Coates. Married Harriette Byers Robinson 1900. Marriage Registration 1900/6489.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 15.9.14 Kingston. Service number: 208. Rank: Private. Roll title: 14th Infantry Battalion (December 1914). Age on enlistment: 37 years. Occupation: Labourer. Marital status: Married. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: wife, Mrs. L. L. Hopkins, Allendale.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 22.12.14 on ship A38 HMAT Ulysses. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 14th Battalion, B Company. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/31/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "12.5.18 returned to Australia on board the ship Gaika. 22.7.18 discharged 3rd Military District as medically unfit. Died 7.6.1943 Creswick. Age at death, 69 years. Death Registration 1943/17452. Place of burial: Creswick Cemetery on 8.6.1943, where he was recorded as a resident of Creswick.",
    "recognition": "1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W73",
