    "notes": "11.7.16 admitted to Military Hospital Fargo (Rollestone, England) with trachoma even though on his enlistments papers he referred to his bad eye sight. Rejoined Battalion 17.11.16. 6.10.16 treated by 6th Australian Field Ambulance Belgium. 7.10.16 treated by 3rd Casualty Clearing Station with bronchitis. 17.11.16 rejoined Battalion in the field. 7.3.17 admitted to hospital with influenza and impetigo. 11.3.17 treated by 6th Australian Field Ambulance for scabies. 31.3.17 discharged for duty. 11.8.17 admitted to 2nd London General Hospital, Chelsea with trachoma. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Johnson from Creswick had been a District Volunteer. Australian National Archives records birth at Ballarat. Death registration records surname as Johnston. On his enlistment papers dated 20.3.16, he indicated that he had previously been rejected because of poor eyesight.",
