    "service": "Joined 15.9.16. Service number: 6324. Rank: Private. Roll title: 24th Infantry Battalion, 13th to 18th Reinforcements (July to November 1916). Age on enlistment: 23 years 4 months. Occupation: Horse Trainer. Address at enlistment: 515 Doveton Street, Ballarat. Marital status: Married. Religion: Church of England. Next of kin and address: wife, Mrs. Eleanor Kay, Harold Street Shepparton. Embarked Melbourne 23.11.16 on ship A20 HMAT Hororata. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 24th Battalion, 18th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/41/4. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
