    "notes": "5.9.17 forfeited 9 days’ pay for being absent without permission. 7.11.17 Field Court Martial – when on active duty deserting His Majesty’s Service on 6.10.17. Appealed that he had been hit in action and wandered away dazed. Found not guilty of desertion but guilty of leave without permission. Sentenced to 2 years with hard labour initially at Military Prison Le Havre. 20.11.17 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Kay was a District Volunteer. 25.5.18 remainder of sentence suspended, discharged to duty. 31.5.18 Wounded in Action. (Severe gunshot wounds to left arm, thigh and knee.) 25.8.18 admitted to Military Hospital, Sutton Veny. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Kay from Springmount had been a District Volunteer. 1.10.19 Medical Report declared soldier unfit for further duty owing to effects of a shell burst which lodged foreign bodies into his left thigh, left knee and left arm.",
