    "service": "Joined 5.10.16 Melbourne. Service number: 750. Rank: Air Mechanic 2nd Class. Roll title: 2nd Australian Flying Squadron, 1st to 4th Reinforcements, (October to December 1916). Age on enlistment: 27 year 11 months. Occupation: Mechanical Engineer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at enlistment: 107 Brougham Street, Ballarat. Next of kin and address: sister, Mrs. Lucy Whatmore, Doveton Street Ballarat. (Both parents deceased.) Embarked Melbourne 25.10.16 on ship A38 HMAT Ulysses. Rate of pay per diem before embarkation: Eight Shillings. Rate of pay per diem after embarkation: Seven Shillings. Original unit: Australian Flying Corps, No. 2 Squadron, C Flight. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 8/5/1.",
    "family": "Born Springmount 20.10.1886. Birth Registration 1886/3924. Father: John Kay. Mother: Annetta Amelia Sonsee.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 5.10.16 Melbourne. Service number: 750. Rank: Air Mechanic 2nd Class. Roll title: 2nd Australian Flying Squadron, 1st to 4th Reinforcements, (October to December 1916). Age on enlistment: 27 year 11 months. Occupation: Mechanical Engineer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at enlistment: 107 Brougham Street, Ballarat. Next of kin and address: sister, Mrs. Lucy Whatmore, Doveton Street Ballarat. (Both parents deceased.)",
