    "additionalNotes": "",
    "notes": "28.7.17 admitted to 8th Field Ambulance with PUO (pyrexia of unknown origin). Same day treated by 56th Casualty Clearing Station. 5.8.17 admitted to University War Hospital, Southampton with trench feet. 31.8.17 transferred to 3rd Auxiliary Hospital, Dartford. 17.6.18 Wounded in Action. Severe gunshot wound to left leg, arm and hand. 4.7.18 taken by ambulance train and admitted to 3rd Auxiliary General Hospital Abbeville. Leg amputated at thigh. 5.7.18 transferred to England on Hospital Ship St. Andrew and admitted to Princess Christian Military Hospital, Englefield Green. 31.7.18 transferred to 2nd Auxiliary Hospital, Southall. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private Kenneally from Broomfield had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser published a list of all from the Borough and Shire who had been Wounded in Action including Private Kenneally.",
