    "service": "Joined 8.7.15 Melbourne. Service number: 898. Rank: Corporal. Roll title: 31st Battalion (November 1915). Age on enlistment: 21 years 7 months. Occupation: Dairyman. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: Mother, Mrs John Kilfoyle, Smeaton, Victoria. Embarked Melbourne 9.11.15 on ship HMAT Wandilla A62. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Six Shillings. Original unit: 31st Battalion. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/48/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Smeaton 1894. Birth Registration 1898/16216. Father: John James Kilfoyle. Mother: Louisa James Harvey.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 8.7.15 Melbourne. Service number: 898. Rank: Corporal. Roll title: 31st Battalion (November 1915). Age on enlistment: 21 years 7 months. Occupation: Dairyman. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: Mother, Mrs John Kilfoyle, Smeaton, Victoria.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 9.11.15 on ship HMAT Wandilla A62. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Six Shillings. Original unit: 31st Battalion. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/48/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "15.3.1917 Killed in Action at Flers, France. Age at death: 23 years. Place of burial: Beaulencourt British Cemetery, Ligny-Thilloy, Picardie, France.",
