    "service": "Joined 27.3.16 Ballarat. Service number: 1690. Rank: Private. Roll title: 39th Infantry Battalion, 1st to 6th Reinforcements, (May to December 1916). Age on enlistment: 19 years 4 months. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at enrolment, c/o Mr. J. J. May, Newlyn. Next of kin and address: Originally his father, Robert McCormack, Tolcon, Loughynn, Dromod County, Leitrim, Ireland. After his father passed away, next of kin was changed to his mother. Embarked Melbourne 27.5.16 on ship A11 HMAT Ascanius. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 39th Battalion, 1st Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/56/2. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Mohill, Ireland c. 1897. Father: Robert McCormack.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 27.3.16 Ballarat. Service number: 1690. Rank: Private. Roll title: 39th Infantry Battalion, 1st to 6th Reinforcements, (May to December 1916). Age on enlistment: 19 years 4 months. Marital status: Single. Religion: Church of England. Address at enrolment, c/o Mr. J. J. May, Newlyn. Next of kin and address: Originally his father, Robert McCormack, Tolcon, Loughynn, Dromod County, Leitrim, Ireland. After his father passed away, next of kin was changed to his mother.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 27.5.16 on ship A11 HMAT Ascanius. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 39th Battalion, 1st Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/56/2. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "25.8.17 returned to Australia. (The hospital ship on which he returned was not disclosed in his file.) 11.1.18 discharged 3rd Military District as medically unfit. 12.4.20 admitted to 11th Australian General Hospital. He died 18.5.1921 of tuberculosis and exhaustion. No relatives were present.",
    "recognition": "British War Medal. Victory Medal. Memorial Scroll. Memorial Plaque. St. Matthew’s Anglican Church Newlyn Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W98",
