    "notes": "29.4.15 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wound to forehead.) Treated at 2nd General Hospital in Egypt. Rejoined 8th Battalion at Gallipoli 26.5.15. 26.7.16 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wound to right leg and buttock.) 1.8.16 evacuated from Rouen for England on board hospital ship HS Aberdonian. 2.8.16 admitted to 3rd West General Hospital Cardiff, Wales. 12.9.16 transferred to 1st Auxiliary Hospital. 16.10.16 discharged direct to hospital ship Karoola for repatriation to Australia. 30.3.17 Private McFarlane was advised that he would be entitled to a pension of 3 pounds 8 shillings as from 29.4.17. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private McFarlane from Springmount had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported all from the Borough and Shire who had been Wounded in Action including Corporal McFarlane (twice).",
