    "fullProfile": "McFarlane, William Henry Family Born Collingwood 1886. Birth Registration 1886/9255. Father: John William McFarlane. Mother: Henrietta Ann Williams. Married Mabel Taylor 24.12.1912. Enlistment Joined 19.8.14 Ballarat. Service number: 324. Rank: Private. Roll title: 8th Infantry Battalion (October 1914). Age on enlistment: 26 years. Occupation: Carter (Ballarat). Marital status: Single. Religion: Methodist. Next of kin and address: John McFarlane, Lewisham Road, Prahran. Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 19.10.14 on ship A24 HMAT Benalla. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 8th Battalion, C Company. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/25/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Additional Notes Private from 19.8.14; Lance Corporal from 8.12.15; Corporal from 26.2.16. Fate 16.10.16 returned to Australia on board the ship Karoola. 28.4.17 discharged 3rd Military District as medically unfit owing to damaged right leg and hip. Died 22.8.1923 Broadmeadows. Age at death, 37 years. Death Registration 1923/9034. Place of burial: Fawkner Memorial Park, Church of England Section on 23.8.23. Recognition 1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. Springmount State School Honour Board. Scrub Hill Uniting Church Newlyn Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W15 Notes 29.4.15 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wound to forehead.) Treated at 2nd General Hospital in Egypt. Rejoined 8th Battalion at Gallipoli 26.5.15. 26.7.16 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wound to right leg and buttock.) 1.8.16 evacuated from Rouen for England on board hospital ship HS Aberdonian. 2.8.16 admitted to 3rd West General Hospital Cardiff, Wales. 12.9.16 transferred to 1st Auxiliary Hospital. 16.10.16 discharged direct to hospital ship Karoola for repatriation to Australia. 30.3.17 Private McFarlane was advised that he would be entitled to a pension of 3 pounds 8 shillings as from 29.4.17. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private McFarlane from Springmount had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported all from the Borough and Shire who had been Wounded in Action including Corporal McFarlane (twice).",
