    "notes": "25.7.16 arrived Plymouth and immediately transferred to 3rd Divisional Train, ASC, Larkhill Camp. 28.5.16 promoted to Staff Sergeant in Australia. 15.9.16 Acting Warrant Officer. Promoted 11.9.17 at Administrative HQ London. 4.12.16 admitted to 3rd London General Hospital – illness undisclosed. Discharged 15.12.16. 19.6.17 departed for France to take up duties with Base Depot at Le Havre. 28.11.17 transferred to AIF Headquarters London from 1st Divisional Train. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Staff Sergeant McGrath from Ballarat had been a District Volunteer. 31.7.34 Melbourne Age reported that D. C. McGrath had died after a long illness. The newspaper also reported that he had been both a State and Federal Politician and that he had been educated at Samuel Fiddian’s Creswick Grammar School. The Grammar School started as a boy’s school but became co-ed after Samuel Fiddian bought the school in 1872.",
