    "service": "Joined 19.9.14 Camperdown. Service number: 428. Rank: Lance Corporal. Roll title: 8th LHR [Light Horse Regiment] (February 1915). Age on enlistment: 26 years 7 months. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Occupation: Station Overseer (Camperdown). Next of kin and address: father, Robert McHutchison, Broomfield. Embarked Melbourne 25.2.15 on ship A16 HMAT Star of Victoria. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 8th Light Horse Regiment, C Squadron. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 10/13/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Broomfield 24.12.1888; Birth Registration 1888/9014. Father: Robert McHutchison. Mother: Mary Evans. Married Carol Daisy Dart 1919. Marriage Registration 1919/2618R.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 19.9.14 Camperdown. Service number: 428. Rank: Lance Corporal. Roll title: 8th LHR [Light Horse Regiment] (February 1915). Age on enlistment: 26 years 7 months. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Occupation: Station Overseer (Camperdown). Next of kin and address: father, Robert McHutchison, Broomfield.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 25.2.15 on ship A16 HMAT Star of Victoria. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 8th Light Horse Regiment, C Squadron. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 10/13/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
