    "location": "Creswick",
    "service": "Joined 21 September 1914 Ararat. Service number: 2794. Rank: Driver. Roll title: 1st Australian Reserve Park 10th Company ASC [Army Service Corps] Reinforcements (December 1914 to January 1916). Age on enlistment: 18 years. Occupation: Farm hand in Ararat. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: Mother, Mrs. R. McKane, Rocky Lead. (For next of kin, soldier wrote: Father + Mother, three brothers at Rocky Lead, Vic.) Embarked Melbourne 22.12.14 on ship A35 HMAT Berrima. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Six Shillings. Original unit: 1st Australian Reserve Park, 1st Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 25/34/2. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born 13.8.98 Bunbury Western Australia. Father: William McKane. Mother: Rita Trotter. Married Jane McLean 1921. Marriage Registration 1921/5786.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 21 September 1914 Ararat. Service number: 2794. Rank: Driver. Roll title: 1st Australian Reserve Park 10th Company ASC [Army Service Corps] Reinforcements (December 1914 to January 1916). Age on enlistment: 18 years. Occupation: Farm hand in Ararat. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: Mother, Mrs. R. McKane, Rocky Lead. (For next of kin, soldier wrote: Father + Mother, three brothers at Rocky Lead, Vic.)",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 22.12.14 on ship A35 HMAT Berrima. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Six Shillings. Original unit: 1st Australian Reserve Park, 1st Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 25/34/2. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "1.11.18 returned to Australia on board the ship Port Lyttelton. 23.2.19 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 17.12.79 Werribee. Age at death, 82 years. Death Registration 1979/28894. Place of burial: Werribee Cemetery.",
    "recognition": "1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E124",
    "commemoration": "",
    "warService": "",
    "nursingService": "",
    "familyConnection": "",
    "additionalNotes": "At the time of his death, he is recorded as being a resident of Werribee and occupation retired. Total effective period of service 1,616 days. Was educated at Rocky Lead State School.",
    "notes": "29.9.14 Driver McKane’s father wrote a letter to Military Officials approving of his son’s enlistment with an age of 18 years and 1 month. It was also signed by his mother. (Letter contains writing similarities to enlistment documents; every likelihood it was written by soldier himself.) 8.6.15 admitted to 17th General Hospital (slight trachoma). 19.7.15 transferred to Mustapha Camp, Egypt. 24.7.15 discharged back to unit. 30.6.15 admitted to 17th General Hospital with conjunctivitis. 2.2.18 detached from 5th Divisional Train to 5th Australian Divisional Reinforcement Wing. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Driver McKane from Rocky Lead had been a District Volunteer. Put his age up from 16 to 18 years to enlist. 29.9.14 both mother and father, writing from Rocky Lead, informed Military Officials that their son was 18 years and 1 month of age.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "McKane, Douglas William Family Born 13.8.98 Bunbury Western Australia. Father: William McKane. Mother: Rita Trotter. Married Jane McLean 1921. Marriage Registration 1921/5786. Enlistment Joined 21 September 1914 Ararat. Service number: 2794. Rank: Driver. Roll title: 1st Australian Reserve Park 10th Company ASC [Army Service Corps] Reinforcements (December 1914 to January 1916). Age on enlistment: 18 years. Occupation: Farm hand in Ararat. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: Mother, Mrs. R. McKane, Rocky Lead. (For next of kin, soldier wrote: Father + Mother, three brothers at Rocky Lead, Vic.) Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 22.12.14 on ship A35 HMAT Berrima. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Six Shillings. Original unit: 1st Australian Reserve Park, 1st Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 25/34/2. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Fate 1.11.18 returned to Australia on board the ship Port Lyttelton. 23.2.19 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 17.12.79 Werribee. Age at death, 82 years. Death Registration 1979/28894. Place of burial: Werribee Cemetery. Recognition 1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E124 Additional Notes At the time of his death, he is recorded as being a resident of Werribee and occupation retired. Total effective period of service 1,616 days. Was educated at Rocky Lead State School. Notes 29.9.14 Driver McKane’s father wrote a letter to Military Officials approving of his son’s enlistment with an age of 18 years and 1 month. It was also signed by his mother. (Letter contains writing similarities to enlistment documents; every likelihood it was written by soldier himself.) 8.6.15 admitted to 17th General Hospital (slight trachoma). 19.7.15 transferred to Mustapha Camp, Egypt. 24.7.15 discharged back to unit. 30.6.15 admitted to 17th General Hospital with conjunctivitis. 2.2.18 detached from 5th Divisional Train to 5th Australian Divisional Reinforcement Wing. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Driver McKane from Rocky Lead had been a District Volunteer. Put his age up from 16 to 18 years to enlist. 29.9.14 both mother and father, writing from Rocky Lead, informed Military Officials that their son was 18 years and 1 month of age.",
