    "additionalNotes": "",
    "notes": "Prior experience: 1 year with Senior Cadets and 2 years with Light Horse. 15.6.16 embarked from Alexandria. 24.6.16 disembarked at Marseilles. 4.6.17 admitted to 8th Field Ambulance with septic gland in neck. Treated by 3rd Casualty Clearing Station. Transferred to 9th General Hospital Rouen, France. 16.6.17 transferred to Base Depot Buchy to convalesce. 7.8.17 discharged to Base Depot. 16.8.17 rejoined unit in the field. 26.7.18 admitted to 8th Field Ambulance with fibrositis and influenza. Treated by 47th Casualty Clearing Station Le Treport, France. 20.1.18 discharged to Base Depot. 9.9.18 rejoined unit in the field. 28.12.18 on leave to Nice until 13.1.19. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Driver McKay from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer. 26.6.19 granted leave in England to engage in nonmilitary employment to gain farming experience before returning to Australia.",
