    "notes": "Prior experience: 3½ years at Bendigo Hospital. 14.1.16 Creswick Advertiser reported that Annie had successfully completed her training at Bendigo Hospital and that her sister was still in training at the same hospital. 19.7.17 disembarked Suez, Egypt. 25.7.17 embarked Port Said, Egypt for Salonika, on board Chargres. 30.7.17 joined 65th General Hospital. 31.5.18 joined 42nd General Hospital. 2.10.18 admitted to 43rd General Hospital Salonika, Greece with conjunctivitis. 22.10.18 discharged to duty. 6.12.18 admitted to 43rd General Hospital with influenza. 24.3.19 taken on strength at AIF Headquarters London. 30.4.19 granted leave for two months in England to attend Mauson’s Motor Training Garage at Westminster, London. 12.7.19 promoted to Sister. 2.8.19 attached to 1st Auxiliary Hospital, Sutton Veny Camp for duty pending repatriation to Australia.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "McKinnon, Sister Annie Family Born Kingston 1891. Birth Registration 1891/24533. Father: Andrew McKinnon. Mother: Mary Ann Archibald. Married John Percy Frederick Wilkinson 1923. Marriage Registration 1923/2042. Enlistment Joined 16.5.17. Rank: Staff Nurse. Roll title: Nurses (July 1915 to November 1918). Age on enlistment: 25 years. Occupation: Trained Nurse. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: father, Mr. A. McKinnon, Kingston Post Office. Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 12.6.17 on ship RMS Mooltan. Rate of pay per diem after embarkation: Seven Shillings and Ten pence. Original unit: Australian Army Nursing Service. Nursing Service Salonika; England Additional Notes 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Staff Nurse McKinnon from Kingston had been a District Volunteer. Middle name recorded as Maud. Fate 1.11.19 returned to Australia on board the ship Nestor. 25.2.20 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 26.2.1970 Ballarat. Age at death, 78 years. Death Registration 1970/4524. Cremated at Ballarat General Cemetery 28.2.1970, remains collected. Recognition British War Medal. Victory Medal. Kingston State School Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W42 Family Military Connections Brother, Private Andrew Charles McKinnon, [No. 323], 8th Infantry Battalion, Killed in Action 19.7.1916. Brother, Private Norman McKinnon, [No. 7553], 8th Infantry Battalion, returned to Australia 13.7.19. Sister, Staff Nurse Ruby McKinnon. [Served in Australia] Cousin, Private James Lindsay Archibald, [No. 677], 14th Infantry Battalion, Killed in Action France, 13.8.16. Notes Prior experience: 3½ years at Bendigo Hospital. 14.1.16 Creswick Advertiser reported that Annie had successfully completed her training at Bendigo Hospital and that her sister was still in training at the same hospital. 19.7.17 disembarked Suez, Egypt. 25.7.17 embarked Port Said, Egypt for Salonika, on board Chargres. 30.7.17 joined 65th General Hospital. 31.5.18 joined 42nd General Hospital. 2.10.18 admitted to 43rd General Hospital Salonika, Greece with conjunctivitis. 22.10.18 discharged to duty. 6.12.18 admitted to 43rd General Hospital with influenza. 24.3.19 taken on strength at AIF Headquarters London. 30.4.19 granted leave for two months in England to attend Mauson’s Motor Training Garage at Westminster, London. 12.7.19 promoted to Sister. 2.8.19 attached to 1st Auxiliary Hospital, Sutton Veny Camp for duty pending repatriation to Australia.",
