    "name": "McLeod, Hugh Harold",
    "gender": "Male",
    "rank": "Private",
    "role": "Soldier",
    "location": "Creswick / Smeaton",
    "service": "Joined 16.3.16. Service number: 1878. Rank: Private. Roll title: 39th Infantry Battalion, 1st to 6th Reinforcements, (May to December 1916). Age on enlistment: 21 years 11 months. Occupation: Labourer (Ballarat). Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: father, Roderick McLeod, Smeaton Post Office. Embarked Melbourne 16.8.16 on ship RMS Orontes. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 39th Battalion, 2nd Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/56/2. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Smeaton 1894. Birth Registration 1894/15606. Father: Roderick McLeod. Mother: Sarah Ann Waddingham.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 16.3.16. Service number: 1878. Rank: Private. Roll title: 39th Infantry Battalion, 1st to 6th Reinforcements, (May to December 1916). Age on enlistment: 21 years 11 months. Occupation: Labourer (Ballarat). Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: father, Roderick McLeod, Smeaton Post Office.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 16.8.16 on ship RMS Orontes. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 39th Battalion, 2nd Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/56/2. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "25.11.17 returned to Australia on board No. 1. Hospital Ship Karoola. 22.2.18 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 11.3.63 Heidelberg. Age at death, 68 years. Death Registration 1963/4934. Place of burial: Creswick Cemetery on 13.3.1963, where he was recorded as a resident of Ballarat.",
    "recognition": "British War Medal. Victory Medal. Smeaton State School Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E104",
    "commemoration": "",
    "warService": "",
    "nursingService": "",
    "familyConnection": "",
    "additionalNotes": "At the time of his death, he was recorded as being a resident of Ballarat and occupation TPI Pensioner. Australian National Archives records birth at Ballarat.",
    "notes": "Prior experience: 3 years with Light Horse Regiment. 10.10.16 joined 39th Battalion in England. 27.11.16 taken on strength of 10th Battalion. 29.5.17 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wounds to head and arm.) Treated by 8th Stationary Hospital Wimereux. 2.6.17 evacuated to England and admitted to Barnett War Hospital. 10.9.17 proceeded overseas to France with unit via Southampton. 6.10.17 Wounded in Action. (Severe gunshot wounds to buttocks.) Treated by 11th Field Ambulance and 44th Casualty Clearing Station. Evacuated to England where he was treated at 1st Auxiliary Military Hospital, Colchester. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private McLeod from Smeaton had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported on all from the Borough and Shire who had been Wounded in Action during WW1 and that included Private McLeod (twice).",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "McLeod, Hugh Harold Family Born Smeaton 1894. Birth Registration 1894/15606. Father: Roderick McLeod. Mother: Sarah Ann Waddingham. Enlistment Joined 16.3.16. Service number: 1878. Rank: Private. Roll title: 39th Infantry Battalion, 1st to 6th Reinforcements, (May to December 1916). Age on enlistment: 21 years 11 months. Occupation: Labourer (Ballarat). Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: father, Roderick McLeod, Smeaton Post Office. Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 16.8.16 on ship RMS Orontes. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 39th Battalion, 2nd Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/56/2. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Fate 25.11.17 returned to Australia on board No. 1. Hospital Ship Karoola. 22.2.18 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 11.3.63 Heidelberg. Age at death, 68 years. Death Registration 1963/4934. Place of burial: Creswick Cemetery on 13.3.1963, where he was recorded as a resident of Ballarat. Recognition British War Medal. Victory Medal. Smeaton State School Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E104 Additional Notes At the time of his death, he was recorded as being a resident of Ballarat and occupation TPI Pensioner. Australian National Archives records birth at Ballarat. Notes Prior experience: 3 years with Light Horse Regiment. 10.10.16 joined 39th Battalion in England. 27.11.16 taken on strength of 10th Battalion. 29.5.17 Wounded in Action. (Gunshot wounds to head and arm.) Treated by 8th Stationary Hospital Wimereux. 2.6.17 evacuated to England and admitted to Barnett War Hospital. 10.9.17 proceeded overseas to France with unit via Southampton. 6.10.17 Wounded in Action. (Severe gunshot wounds to buttocks.) Treated by 11th Field Ambulance and 44th Casualty Clearing Station. Evacuated to England where he was treated at 1st Auxiliary Military Hospital, Colchester. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private McLeod from Smeaton had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported on all from the Borough and Shire who had been Wounded in Action during WW1 and that included Private McLeod (twice).",
