    "enlistment": "Joined 17.7.15 Melbourne. Service number: 2084. Rank: Private. Roll title: 24th Infantry Battalion, 1st to 8th Reinforcements (May 1915 to January 1916). Age on enlistment: 38 years 8 months. Occupation: Telegraph Linesman (Melbourne). Marital status: Single. Religion: Roman Catholic. Next of kin and address: mother, Mrs. J. McMahon, Newlyn Post Office, later 16 Bloom Street Moonee Ponds. (Father deceased.)",
    "embarkation": "Embarked 26.8.15 on ship A68 HMAT Anchises. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 24th Battalion, 3rd Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/41/2. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
