    "notes": "12.10.15 taken on strength at Gallipoli. 20.3.16 departed Alexandria, Egypt to join BEF [British Expeditionary Force] France. 20.3.16 disembarked at Marseilles. 3.2.17 attached for duty in France. 10.2.17 taken on strength of 6th Machine Gun Company from 24th Battalion. 27.8.18 on leave to England until 14.9.18. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private McMahon from Blampied had been a District Volunteer. 13.2.19 embarked Le Havre, France for Weymouth to join the 2nd Training Brigade and await repatriation to Australia. 13.4.19 transferred to 2nd Machine Gun Battalion.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "McMahon, James Family Born Smeaton 1876. Birth Registration 1876/25980. Father: John McMahon. Mother: Honora Dwyer. Enlistment Joined 17.7.15 Melbourne. Service number: 2084. Rank: Private. Roll title: 24th Infantry Battalion, 1st to 8th Reinforcements (May 1915 to January 1916). Age on enlistment: 38 years 8 months. Occupation: Telegraph Linesman (Melbourne). Marital status: Single. Religion: Roman Catholic. Next of kin and address: mother, Mrs. J. McMahon, Newlyn Post Office, later 16 Bloom Street Moonee Ponds. (Father deceased.) Embarkation Embarked 26.8.15 on ship A68 HMAT Anchises. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 24th Battalion, 3rd Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/41/2. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Fate 13.4.19 returned to Australia aboard the Castalia from Devonport. 16.5.19 discharged 3rd Military District as medically unfit. Unconfirmed but he may have died in 1949 at Point Lonsdale. Recognition 1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. Smeaton State School Honour Board. Kangaroo Hills State School Honour Board. Kooroocheang State School Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E99 Notes 12.10.15 taken on strength at Gallipoli. 20.3.16 departed Alexandria, Egypt to join BEF [British Expeditionary Force] France. 20.3.16 disembarked at Marseilles. 3.2.17 attached for duty in France. 10.2.17 taken on strength of 6th Machine Gun Company from 24th Battalion. 27.8.18 on leave to England until 14.9.18. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private McMahon from Blampied had been a District Volunteer. 13.2.19 embarked Le Havre, France for Weymouth to join the 2nd Training Brigade and await repatriation to Australia. 13.4.19 transferred to 2nd Machine Gun Battalion.",
