    "additionalNotes": "Was employed by John Leishman as a farm assistant.",
    "notes": "Prior experience: 3 years with 71st Infantry. 10.6.16 treated by 12th Field Ambulance for influenza before being transferred to 12th Casualty Clearing Station Merris, France. Admitted to 2nd Australian General Hospital Mousset for 2 weeks. 11.4.17 first reported as Missing in Action. 26.11.17 Court of Enquiry determined that Private McMillan had been Killed in Action. Also recorded that his will had not been received. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private McMillan from Wallacetown had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser published a list of all from the Borough and Shire who had been Killed in Action including Private McMillan. Cemetery details from AIF record his name as Henry Alexander MacMillan. In some records he was known as William Henry McMillan.",
