    "notes": "6.1.16 Taunton, forfeited 2 days’ pay for being absent without permission. 10.12.16 when on active duty, neglected to obey Battalion Orders. Was admonished by Major McDonald. 16.12.16 promoted to Corporal with 54th Battery. 28.2.17 evacuated to England via 1st Canadian General Hospital, Etaples France with deafness and tonsillitis. Embarked from Calais. Admitted to 3rd Auxiliary General Hospital Brighton, England. 27.4.17 transferred to 1st Auxiliary Hospital. 12.5.17 granted furlough until 25.5.17. 22.7.17 returned to Australia with continued deafness. 6.11.17 granted a pension of one pound fourteen shillings per fortnight. 2.2.18 his wife was granted a pension of seventeen shillings per fortnight. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Gunner McPhee from Blampied had been a District Volunteer.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "McPhee, Edward Alexander Family Born Blampied 1891. Birth Registration 1891/8295. Father: Daniel McPhee. Mother: Jane Learmonth. Married Florence Elva Wallis 1918. Marriage Registration 1918/1617. Enlistment Joined 7.6.15. Service number: 58. Rank: Gunner. Roll title: SAB [Siege Artillery Brigade] and 1st Reinforcements (July 1915). Age on enlistment: 24 years. Occupation: Tramway Employee. Address at date of enlistment: Victoria Barracks Brisbane. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: father, D. McPhee, “Renfrew,” Blampied. Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 17.7.15 1915 on ship A67 HMAT Orsova. Rate of pay per diem before Embarkation: Five Shillings. Rate of pay per diem after Embarkation: Six Shillings. Original unit: Siege Artillery Brigade. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 13/49/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Fate 22.7.17 returned to Australia on board ship HS Nestor. 5.11.17 discharged 3rd Military District. Died 1.6.50 Ballarat. Age at death, 59 years. Death Registration 1950/17978. Place of burial: Ballarat (New) Cemetery on 2.6.1950. Recognition British War Medal. Victory Medal. Allendale State School Honour Board. Plaque in Victorian Garden of Remembrance. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree W60 Notes 6.1.16 Taunton, forfeited 2 days’ pay for being absent without permission. 10.12.16 when on active duty, neglected to obey Battalion Orders. Was admonished by Major McDonald. 16.12.16 promoted to Corporal with 54th Battery. 28.2.17 evacuated to England via 1st Canadian General Hospital, Etaples France with deafness and tonsillitis. Embarked from Calais. Admitted to 3rd Auxiliary General Hospital Brighton, England. 27.4.17 transferred to 1st Auxiliary Hospital. 12.5.17 granted furlough until 25.5.17. 22.7.17 returned to Australia with continued deafness. 6.11.17 granted a pension of one pound fourteen shillings per fortnight. 2.2.18 his wife was granted a pension of seventeen shillings per fortnight. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Gunner McPhee from Blampied had been a District Volunteer.",
