    "service": "Joined 23.7.15 Ballarat. Service number: 7988. Rank: Driver. Roll title: 8th Infantry Brigade Train, 18th Company ASC [Army Service Corps] (November 1915). Age on enlistment: 20 years. Occupation: Farmer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: father, C. McPherson, Post Office Newlyn, via Ballarat. Embarked Melbourne 5.11.15 on ship A41 HMAT Bakara. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Six Shillings. Original unit: 8th Infantry Brigade Train. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 25/37/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Dean 1895. Birth Registration 1895/11460. Father: Charles McPherson. Mother: Clara Adelaide Rickey. Married Doris Caroline King 1925. Marriage Registration 1925/4065.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 23.7.15 Ballarat. Service number: 7988. Rank: Driver. Roll title: 8th Infantry Brigade Train, 18th Company ASC [Army Service Corps] (November 1915). Age on enlistment: 20 years. Occupation: Farmer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: father, C. McPherson, Post Office Newlyn, via Ballarat.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne 5.11.15 on ship A41 HMAT Bakara. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Six Shillings. Original unit: 8th Infantry Brigade Train. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 25/37/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
    "fate": "2.6.19 returned to Australia on board the ship Beltana from Devonport. 10.9.19 discharged 3rd Military District. No Victorian death registration located.",
