    "notes": "Prior experience: Melbourne University Rifles and 71st Battalion. 26.7.15 both his father and mother wrote to Military Authorities informing them of their approval for their son to enlist. 16.10.15 commenced as a Driver for 18th Company ASC [Army Service Corps]. 16.6.16 departed Alexandria, Egypt to join BEF [British Expeditionary Force] France. 23.6.16 disembarked Marseilles from the Tunisian. 21.8.17 admitted to 8th Australian Field Ambulance France with abscess on foot. 24.8.17 discharged back to unit for duty. 4.2.18 on leave to England until 20.2.18. 3.10.18 on leave in France until 18.10.18. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Driver McPherson from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer. 17.4.19 returned from France to England to prepare for repatriation to Australia.",
    "militaryMedalCitation": "",
    "fullProfile": "McPherson, William Ogilvy Family Born Dean 1895. Birth Registration 1895/11460. Father: Charles McPherson. Mother: Clara Adelaide Rickey. Married Doris Caroline King 1925. Marriage Registration 1925/4065. Enlistment Joined 23.7.15 Ballarat. Service number: 7988. Rank: Driver. Roll title: 8th Infantry Brigade Train, 18th Company ASC [Army Service Corps] (November 1915). Age on enlistment: 20 years. Occupation: Farmer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: father, C. McPherson, Post Office Newlyn, via Ballarat. Embarkation Embarked Melbourne 5.11.15 on ship A41 HMAT Bakara. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Six Shillings. Original unit: 8th Infantry Brigade Train. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 25/37/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas. Fate 2.6.19 returned to Australia on board the ship Beltana from Devonport. 10.9.19 discharged 3rd Military District. No Victorian death registration located. Recognition 1914–15 Star. British War Medal. Victory Medal. Scrub Hill Uniting Church Newlyn Honour Board. Newlyn Methodist Church Honour Board. RSL Virtual War Memorial. Avenue of Honour Tree E50 Notes Prior experience: Melbourne University Rifles and 71st Battalion. 26.7.15 both his father and mother wrote to Military Authorities informing them of their approval for their son to enlist. 16.10.15 commenced as a Driver for 18th Company ASC [Army Service Corps]. 16.6.16 departed Alexandria, Egypt to join BEF [British Expeditionary Force] France. 23.6.16 disembarked Marseilles from the Tunisian. 21.8.17 admitted to 8th Australian Field Ambulance France with abscess on foot. 24.8.17 discharged back to unit for duty. 4.2.18 on leave to England until 20.2.18. 3.10.18 on leave in France until 18.10.18. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Driver McPherson from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer. 17.4.19 returned from France to England to prepare for repatriation to Australia.",
