    "additionalNotes": "",
    "notes": "Prior experience: service with 20th Light Horse Regiment. 28.12.14 forfeited seven days’ pay for “Conduct to the prejudice of good order and discipline” by refusing to obey an order. 29.7.15 Wounded in Action at Gaba Tepe, Gallipoli. 31.7.15 died on board hospital ship Rewa off the Gallipoli Peninsula where he was being treated for shrapnel wounds to the head. 31.7.15 Buried at Sea by Reverend G. L. Kellan. 19.1.17 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private May had been Killed in Action. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private May from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser published a list of all from the Borough and Shire who had been Killed in Action including Private May. 3.7.22 medals, memorial plaque and memorial scroll were sent to his father as next of kin.",
