    "service": "Joined 23.7.15 Ballarat. Service number: 7986. Rank: Driver. Roll title: 8th Infantry Brigade Train, 18th Company ASC [Army Service Corps] (November 1915). Age on enlistment: 23 years. Occupation: Farmer. Marital status: Single. Religion: Presbyterian. Next of kin and address: father, George May, Newlyn Post Office. Embarked Melbourne 5.11.15 on ship A41 HMAT Bakara. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Six Shillings. Original unit: 8th Infantry Brigade Train, 18th Company, Australian Army Service Corps. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 25/37/1. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
