    "notes": "16.6.16 joined BEF [British Expeditionary Force] at Alexandria, Egypt. 23.6.16 disembarked at Marseilles, France for duty with 18th ASC [Army Service Corps]. 24.8.17 on leave to England until 3.9.17. 17.3.19 on leave to England until 4.1.19. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported that Private May from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer. 2.11.18 on leave in France until 15.11.18. 17.4.19 disembarked at Weymouth from France, to prepare for repatriation to Australia. Family Military Connections Brother, Private Douglas George May, [No. 6558], 8th Infantry Battalion, Died of Wounds, Belgium, 21.9.17. Brother, Lieutenant Henry Vickery May, [No. 6559], 8th Infantry Battalion, returned to Australia 20.6.19.",
