    "notes": "2.2.17 proceeded to France from Folkestone aboard the Victoria. 10.2.17 taken on strength of 8th Battalion from 21st Reinforcements. 21.9.17 Wounded in Action. (Very severe shell wounds to head and listed as being critical.) Admitted to 6th Australian Field Ambulance. Died 21.9.17 at 17th Casualty Clearing Station, Belgium. 3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser reported 3rd December 1918 that Private May from Newlyn had been a District Volunteer. 31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser published a list of all from the Borough and Shire who had been Killed in Action including Private May. Medals as well as the Memorial Plaque and Memorial Scroll were forwarded to Private May’s father as his next of kin. Family Military Connections Brother, Driver Archie May, [No. 7986], 8th Infantry Brigade, Australian Army Service Corps, returned to Australia 19.7.1919. Brother, Lieutenant Henry Vickery May, [No. 6559], 8th Infantry Battalion, returned to Australia 20.6.1919.",
