    "service": "Joined 7.12.16 Ballarat. Service number: 7266. Rank: Private. Roll title: 6th Infantry Battalion, 24th and 25th Reinforcements, (February to August 1917). Age on enlistment: 29 years 3 months. Occupation: Storekeeper. Marital status: Single. Religion: Methodist. Next of kin and address: mother, Mrs. Mary Ann Merritt, North Creswick. Embarked Melbourne 19.2.17 on ship A70 HMAT Ballarat. Rate of pay per diem before and after embarkation: Five Shillings. Original unit: 6th Battalion, 24th Reinforcement. Australian War Memorial Embarkation Roll Number: 23/23/6. Later in this publication are more details about the ships that took individuals overseas.",
