    "notes": "Prior experience: three years\nwith Senior Cadets.\n13.3.16 transferred to 14th\nField Artillery Brigade at Tel-\nel-Kebir, Egypt.\n16.7.16 treated by 15th\nField\nAmbulance after horse fell\non him. 21.7.16 admitted to\n30th\nGeneral Hospital, Calais\nFrance with back injury.\n13.8.16 embarked Calais on\nboard HS Brighton for\nEngland.\n29.12.16 Court of Inquiry\nfound that injury occurred\nwhen horse Mineall was\nriding reared and fell on him.\nNo blame attributed to\nMineall.\n19.12.16 returned to\nAustralian General Base\nDepot, Etaples France.\n15.1.17 posted to 54th\nBattery 14th\nField Artillery\nBrigade.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Private Mineall\nfrom Rocky Lead had been a\nDistrict Volunteer.\n31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\npublished a list of all from\nthe Borough and Shire who\nhad been Killed in Action\nincluding Gunner Mineall.\nEnlistment papers record his\nbirth as Wombah, NSW.",
