    "notes": "Prior experience with Senior\nCadets.\n25.4.17 arrived Devonport,\nEngland.\n18.7.17 treated at the\nMilitary Hospital Sutton Veny\nCamp for illness.\n5.9.17 from 2nd\nTraining\nBattalion proceeded\noverseas to France from\nSouthampton.\n8.9.17 Found guilty of\nconduct to the prejudice of\ngood order and military\ndiscipline in that he failed to\nappear on 6.45am parade on\n4.9.17. Forfeited 7 days'\npay. Penalty imposed by\nCaptain Bond.\n24.9.17 admitted to hospital\nwith right ankle joint painful.\n7.10.17 admitted to 3rd\nLondon General Hospital\nwith pneumonia –\nconsidered dangerously ill.\n13.3.18 admitted to Bulford\nMilitary Hospital.\n30.3.18 caught playing an\nillegal gambling game.\nAdmonished, however\ncharge dismissed by Lt.\nColonel Stewart.\n8.4.18 discharged from\nhospital.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Private\nMitchell from Smeaton had\nbeen a District Volunteer.",
