    "fullProfile": "Mitchell, Herbert\nFamily\nBorn Blampied 1887. Birth\nRegistration 1887/30540. Father:\nRobert Mitchell. Mother:\nMary Ann Tyzzer.\nEnlistment\nJoined 30.7.15 Ballarat.\nService number: 8955. Rank:\nDriver. Roll title: 2nd\nDivisional Ammunition\nColumn (November 1915).\nAge on enlistment: 27 years\n10 months. Occupation:\nBlacksmith. Marital status:\nSingle. Religion:\nPresbyterian. Next of kin and\naddress: father, R. Mitchell,\nBlampied via Newlyn.\nEmbarkation\nEmbarked Melbourne\n16.11.15 on ship A39 HMAT\nPort MacQuarie. Rate of pay\nper diem before and after\nembarkation: Six Shillings.\nOriginal unit: 2nd\nDivisional\nAmmunition Column.\nAustralian War Memorial\nEmbarkation Roll Number:\n25/90/1.\nLater in this publication are more\ndetails about the ships that took\nindividuals overseas.\nFate\n27.4.19 returned to Australia\non board the ship Runic.\n2.8.19 discharged 3rd\nMilitary\nDistrict.\nDied 4.7.60 Cranbourne. Age\nat death, 72 years. Death\nRegistration 1960/8587. Place of\nburial: Springvale Botanical\nCemetery where he was\ncremated on 6.7.60.\nRecognition\n• 1914–15 Star.\n• British War Medal.\n• Victory Medal.\n• Mount Prospect State\nSchool Honour Board.\n• Mount Prospect\nPresbyterian Church\nHonour Board.\n• RSL Virtual War\nMemorial.\nAvenue of Honour Tree W14\nAdditional Notes\nAt the time of his death, he\nwas recorded as a resident\nof Mount Prospect with\noccupation of farmer.\nAfter the war, was granted\nsoldier settlement block at\nRocky Lead.\nNotes\nHad served apprenticeship\nwith his father for four years\ntraining to be a Blacksmith.\n18.12.15 disembarked Suez,\nEgypt and proceeded to join\nMEF [Mediterranean\nExpeditionary Force].\n10.3.16 transferred to 22nd\nHowitzer Brigade at\nMoascar, Egypt.\n18.3.16 departed Alexandria,\nEgypt to join BEF [British\nExpeditionary Force] France.\n25.3.16 arrived Marseilles.\n30.4.16 Driver with 22nd\nHowitzer Brigade.\nShoeing Smith from 1.5.16.\n7.5.16 admitted to 7th\nField\nAmbulance with bronchitis.\n13.5.16 rejoined unit.\n3.5.17 taken on strength of\n4th\nArtillery Brigade from\n104th\nBattery.\n8.8.16 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Driver Mitchell\nwas a District Volunteer.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Driver Mitchell\nfrom Blampied had been a\nDistrict Volunteer.\n27.2.19 returned from\nFrance to prepare for\nrepatriation to Australia.",
