    "fullProfile": "Murphy, John Spence\nFamily\nBorn Springmount 1888. Birth\nRegistration 1888/12754. Father:\nPatrick Murphy. Mother:\nJane Gutherie Slade. Married\nAlice Maud Bailey 1915.\nMarriage Registration 1915/10391.\nEnlistment\nJoined 10.7.15 Melbourne.\nService number: 882. Rank:\nPrivate. Roll title: 29th\nInfantry Battalion\n(November 1915). Age on\nenlistment: 27 years.\nOccupation: Labourer.\nMarital status: Married.\nReligion: Roman Catholic.\nOriginal next of kin and\naddress: mother, Mrs. Jane\nMurphy Springmount but\nlater changed to wife, Mrs.\nAlice Maud Murphy, Wattle\nFlat Post Office via Ballarat.\nEmbarkation\nEmbarked Melbourne\n10.11.15 on ship A11 HMAT\nAscanius. Rate of pay per\ndiem before and after\nembarkation: Five Shillings.\nOriginal unit: 29th\nBattalion,\nC Company. Australian War\nMemorial Embarkation Roll\nNumber: 23/46/1.\nLater in this publication are more\ndetails about the ships that took\nindividuals overseas.\nFate\n21.3.19 return to Australia\non board the ship Kildonian\nCastle from Devonport.\n29.6.19 discharged 3rd\nMilitary District.\nDied 12.7.1959. Age at\ndeath, 71 years. Death\nRegistration 1959/25199. Place of\nburial: Creswick Cemetery on\n14.7.1959, where he was\nrecorded as a resident of\nSpringmount.\nRecognition\n• 1914–15 Star.\n• British War Medal.\n• Victory Medal.\n• Springmount State\nSchool Honour Board.\n• RSL Virtual War\nMemorial.\nAvenue of Honour Tree W111\nAdditional Notes\nNext of kin details originally\nrecorded his mother but\nchanged to his wife upon\nmarriage in 1915.\nNotes\n21.7.15 part of 60th\nCompany\nDepot, Seymour.\n7.12.15 arrived Suez, Egypt.\n16.6.16 departed Alexandria,\nEgypt to join BEF [British\nExpeditionary Force] France.\n23.6.16 arrived Marseilles.\n25.10.17 admitted to 1st\nANZAC Cookery School in the\nfield. 1.11.17 rejoined unit.\n12.10.18 transferred to 32nd\nBattalion while on leave.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Private\nMurphy from Springmount\nhad been a District\nVolunteer.\n10.1.19 embarked from Le\nHavre France for England to\nawait return to Australia.\n23.1.19 transferred to Sutton\nVeny Camp then to 2nd\nTraining Brigade Codford\nCamp.\nFamily Military Connection\nBrother, Private, Murphy,\nJames Maxwell, [No. 885], 29th\nInfantry Battalion, returned to\nAustralia 13.4.19.\nWar Service\nEgypt; Western Front",
