    "notes": "25.1.16 taken on strength at\nTel-el-Kebir, Egypt with 8th\nBattalion.\n28.10.16 penalised 7 days'\nfield punishment for\ndisobedience in not saluting\nan officer.\n2.4.17 taken on strength of\n3rd\nArmy Field Artillery\nBrigade.\n30.12.17 to 14.1.18 on leave\nto England.\n19.7.18 treated by 15th\nAustralian Field Ambulance\nfor jaw injury. Transferred\nto 20th\nCasualty Clearing\nStation. 22.7.18 admitted to\n5th\nGeneral Hospital Rouen,\nFrance. 23.7.18 embarked\nfor England. 25.7.18\nadmitted to 1st\nSouth\nGeneral Hospital Edgbaston\nwith severely fractured\nlower jaw. 7.9.18 discharged\nto report to Queen's\nHospital, Frognal, Sidcup.\n12.9.18 discharged to report\nto No. 2 Camp.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Private Phillips\nfrom Portland had been a\nDistrict Volunteer.\n15.1.19 transferred for duty\nto Administrative HQ London\npending repatriation to\nAustralia.",
