    "fullProfile": "Phillips, Stanley Gordon\nFamily\nBorn Dean 1894. Birth\nRegistration 1894/11172. Father:\nWilliam Phillips. Mother:\nElizabeth Davey. Married\nVeronica Helen Burn 28.9.18,\nSt. George Hanover Square\nRegistry Office London.\nMarriage Registration ME1544.\nMarried again in Victoria in\n1928. Marriage Registration\n1928/11455.\nEnlistment\nJoined 23.6.15 Melbourne.\nService number: 2660. Rank:\nPrivate. Roll title: 5th\nBattalion, 8th\nReinforcement.\nAge on enlistment: 21 years\n3 months. Occupation:\nFarmer. Marital status:\nSingle. Religion: Methodist.\nNext of kin and address:\nfather, William Phillips,\nGoral, West Portland.\nEmbarkation\nEmbarked Melbourne\n15.9.15 on ship SS Makarini.\nAustralian War Memorial\nEmbarkation Roll Number:\n23/22/2.\nLater in this publication are more\ndetails about the ships that took\nindividuals overseas.\nFate\n28.9.19 returned to Australia\non board the ship HT\nOsterley with his wife.\n27.1.20 discharged 3rd\nMilitary District.\nDied 30.7.65 Ballarat. Age at\ndeath, 70 years. Death\nRegistration 1965/16942. Place of\nburial: Ballarat (New)\nCemetery.\nRecognition\n• 1914–15 Star.\n• British War Medal.\n• Victory Medal.\n• Dean State School\nHonour Board.\n• RSL Virtual War\nMemorial.\nAvenue of Honour Tree W131\nAdditional Notes\nAt the time of his death, he\nwas recorded as being a\nresident of Portland with\noccupation retired farmer.\nNotes\n25.1.16 taken on strength at\nTel-el-Kebir, Egypt with 8th\nBattalion.\n28.10.16 penalised 7 days'\nfield punishment for\ndisobedience in not saluting\nan officer.\n2.4.17 taken on strength of\n3rd\nArmy Field Artillery\nBrigade.\n30.12.17 to 14.1.18 on leave\nto England.\n19.7.18 treated by 15th\nAustralian Field Ambulance\nfor jaw injury. Transferred\nto 20th\nCasualty Clearing\nStation. 22.7.18 admitted to\n5th\nGeneral Hospital Rouen,\nFrance. 23.7.18 embarked\nfor England. 25.7.18\nadmitted to 1st\nSouth\nGeneral Hospital Edgbaston\nwith severely fractured\nlower jaw. 7.9.18 discharged\nto report to Queen's\nHospital, Frognal, Sidcup.\n12.9.18 discharged to report\nto No. 2 Camp.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Private Phillips\nfrom Portland had been a\nDistrict Volunteer.\n15.1.19 transferred for duty\nto Administrative HQ London\npending repatriation to\nAustralia.",
