    "service": "Joined 4.8.15 Melbourne.\nService number: 3863. Rank:\nPrivate. Roll title: 14th\nInfantry\nBattalion, 5th\nto 12th\nReinforcements (April to\nNovember 1915). Age on\nenlistment: 22 years.\nOccupation: Law Clerk. Marital\nstatus: Single. Religion: Roman\nCatholic. Next of kin and\naddress: mother, Mrs. Kate\nPrendergast, 27 Mascoma\nStreet, Ascot Vale. Embarked Melbourne\n23.11.15 on ship A40 HMAT\nCeramic. Rate of pay per diem\nbefore and after embarkation:\nFive Shillings. Original unit:\n14th\nBattalion, 12th\nReinforcement. Australian\nWar Memorial Embarkation\nRoll Number: 23/31/3.\nLater in this publication are more\ndetails about the ships that took\nindividuals overseas.\nMention in Despatches\nAwarded, and promulgated,\nLondon Gazette, second\nSupplement, No. 30107, dated\n1.6.1917; Commonwealth\nGazette No. 169, dated\n4.10.1917.",
    "family": "Born Newlyn 20.8.1893.\nfather: Thomas Prendergast.\nMother: Catherine Rush.\nMarried Mary Agnes Mulcahy\n10.12.1921 at Kensington, VIC.\nMarriage Registration 1921/11412.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 4.8.15 Melbourne.\nService number: 3863. Rank:\nPrivate. Roll title: 14th\nInfantry\nBattalion, 5th\nto 12th\nReinforcements (April to\nNovember 1915). Age on\nenlistment: 22 years.\nOccupation: Law Clerk. Marital\nstatus: Single. Religion: Roman\nCatholic. Next of kin and\naddress: mother, Mrs. Kate\nPrendergast, 27 Mascoma\nStreet, Ascot Vale.",
