    "fullProfile": "Rasmussen, Carl\nFamily\nBorn Lal Lal 7.5.1875. Birth\nRegistration 1875/7851. Father:\nCarl (Charles) Rasmussen.\nMother: Catherine Jane\nRicketts. Married Eunice\nPollard 1896 Ballarat. Marriage\nRegistration 1896/6129.\nEnlistment\nJoined 19.7.15 Melbourne.\nService number: 4872. Rank:\nPrivate. Roll title: 8th\nInfantry Battalion, 13th\nto\n23rd\nReinforcements\n(December 1915 to\nNovember 1916). Age on\nenlistment: 40 years.\nOccupation: Blacksmith.\nMarital status: Married.\nReligion: Church of England.\nNext of kin and address:\nwife, Mrs. Eunice\nRasmussen, Rocky Lead.\nEmbarkation\nEmbarked Melbourne 7.3.16\non ship A18 HMAT Wiltshire.\nRate of pay per diem before\nand after embarkation: Five\nShillings. Original unit: 8th\nBattalion, 15th\nReinforcement. Australian\nWar Memorial Embarkation\nRoll Number: 23/25/5.\nAdditional Notes\nPrivate Rasmussen wrote on\nhis enlistment papers that he\nand his wife had 7 children.\nFate\n8.5.19 returned to Australia\non board the ship Devanha.\n23.10.19 discharged 3rd\nMilitary District.\nDied 11.5.1960 Heidelberg.\nAge at death, 85 years. Death\nRegistration 1960/5945.\nRecognition\n• British War Medal.\n• Victory Medal.\n• RSL Virtual War\nMemorial.\nAvenue of Honour Tree E102\nAdditional Notes\nAt the time of his death, he\nwas recorded as being a\nresident of Coburg with\noccupation ex cabinet\nmaker.\nDied at the Heidelberg\nCommonwealth Repatriation\nHospital.\nLater in this publication are more\ndetails about the ships that took\nindividuals overseas.\nNotes\n17.4.16 taken on strength of\n5th\npioneer Division at Tel-el-\nKebir, Egypt.\n19.6.16 departed Alexandria,\nEgypt to join BEF [British\nExpeditionary Force] France.\n26.6.16 arrived Marseilles.\n10.2.17 forfeited 1 day's pay\nfor not obeying Battalion\ncensorship regulations in\nletters. Penalty imposed by\nCommanding Officer of 5th\nPioneer Battalion.\n17.4.18 Wounded in Action\nFrance. (Serious gas\npoisoning.) 23.4.18\nadmitted to 3rd\nSouthern\nGeneral Hospital, Oxford.\n26.6.18 AIF wrote to his wife\ninforming her that her\nhusband was now\nconvalescing.\n27.8.18 rejoined unit.\n30.9.18 Wounded in Action\nfor a second time while\nserving with 5th\nPioneer\nBattalion. (Nature of\nwounding not disclosed.)\nDischarged from hospital\n1.10.18.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Private\nRasmussen from Rocky Lead\nhad been a District\nVolunteer.",
