    "notes": "24.6.16 disembarked at\nMarseilles.\n8.12.16 Mentioned in Orders\n“when his comrade's horses\nbecame reactive and bolted\nunder hostile shell fire, he\nturned back to rescue his\ncomrade who had been\nthrown and injured, and took\nhim to a safe place, then he\nreturned to recover the\nremaining horses.”\n3.1.17 admitted to 38th\nCasualty Clearing Station\nwith PUO (pyrexia of\nunknown origin). 6.1.17\nadmitted to 5th\nGeneral\nHospital Rouen, France.\n13.1.17 evacuated to\nEngland on board hospital\nship St. Patrick. 16.2.17\ndischarged and granted\nfurlough to 5.3.17.\n2.6.17 forfeited 14 days' pay\nfor being in the Sergeants'\nMess during prohibited\nhours. Punishment imposed\nby Lieutenant Colonel Lamb.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Private\nRedman from Broomfield\nhad been a District\nVolunteer.\nAustralian National Archives\nrecords birth at Talbot.",
