    "notes": "Prior Service – 3 years with\n19th\nAustralian Light Horse\nRegiment.\n13.5.16 taken on strength of\n3rd\nLight Horse Regiment at\nTel-el-Kebir, Egypt.\n10.12.16 penalised with 60\ndays' field punishment for a\nnumber of offences including\nbeing drunk while on active\nservice and attempting to\nescape from custody.\n26.1.17 returned to unit\nafter detention.\n21.8.17 transferred to\nRailway Construction School,\nEl Kantara, Egypt. 27.8.17\nreturned to unit.\n18.11.17 Died of Wounds.\n(Severe gassing.) Buried by\nChaplain F.H. King in\nroadside grave. 19.1.20,\nbody was exhumed and\nreinterred in Ramleh Military\nCemetery Palestine. The\nwork was carried out “with\nevery measure of care and\nreverence in the presence of\na Chaplain”.\nOriginal burial service was\npresided over by Reverend\nF.H. King, Church of England.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Private\nRedman from Sulky Gully\nhad been a District\nVolunteer.",
