    "location": "Creswick / Smeaton",
    "service": "Joined 22.5.16. Service\nnumber: 2198. Rank: Private.\nRoll title: 39th\nInfantry\nBattalion, 1st\nto 6th\nReinforcements, (May to\nDecember 1916). Age on\nenlistment: 24 years 3\nmonths. Occupation: Miner.\nMarital status: Single.\nAddress at date of\nenlistment: Ararat. Religion:\nMethodist. Next of kin and\naddress: mother, Mrs.\nElizabeth Cowan, Smeaton\nPost Office. (Father\ndeceased). Embarked Melbourne\n25.9.16 on ship A9 HMAT\nShropshire. Rate of pay per\ndiem before and after\nembarkation: Five Shillings.\nOriginal unit: 39th\nBattalion,\n3rd\nReinforcement.\nAustralian War Memorial\nEmbarkation Roll Number:\n23/56/2.",
    "family": "Born Smeaton 1892. Birth\nRegistration 1892/7968. Father:\nRobert Fowler Waddingham.\nMother: Elizabeth Mary\nJones. Married Edna Lillian\nWilson in 1920 at\nMerewether, NSW.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 22.5.16. Service\nnumber: 2198. Rank: Private.\nRoll title: 39th\nInfantry\nBattalion, 1st\nto 6th\nReinforcements, (May to\nDecember 1916). Age on\nenlistment: 24 years 3\nmonths. Occupation: Miner.\nMarital status: Single.\nAddress at date of\nenlistment: Ararat. Religion:\nMethodist. Next of kin and\naddress: mother, Mrs.\nElizabeth Cowan, Smeaton\nPost Office. (Father\ndeceased).",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne\n25.9.16 on ship A9 HMAT\nShropshire. Rate of pay per\ndiem before and after\nembarkation: Five Shillings.\nOriginal unit: 39th\nBattalion,\n3rd\nReinforcement.\nAustralian War Memorial\nEmbarkation Roll Number:\n23/56/2.",
    "fate": "5.4.18 Died of Wounds while\nserving with the 39th\nInfantry\nBattalion, Buire, Somme\nSector, France. Age at death,\n26 years. Place of burial:\nQuerrieu British Cemetery,\n(Row A, Grave Number 9),\nFrance.",
    "recognition": "• British War Medal.\n• Victory Medal.\n• Memorial Plaque.\n• Memorial Scroll.\n• RSL Virtual War\nMemorial.\n• Smeaton State School\nHonour Board.\n• Kangaroo Hills State\nSchool Honour Board.\n• District of Ullina\nCommemorative Stone.\n• Ullina State School\nHonour Board.\n• Kooroocheang State\nSchool Honour Board.\nAvenue of Honour Tree W82",
