    "additionalNotes": "Privates E. B. Warren, H.\nDean and W. O'Rourke were\ninvited to a welcome home\nparty in the Dean Hall. E. B.\nWarren was the only one\nable to attend. A very large\naudience saw presentations\nof certificates and medals,\nwith a concert and supper.",
    "notes": "Prior experience: 14 years\nwith Rifle Club.\n15.9.16 joined 2nd\nTraining\nBattalion.\n12.12.16 reported to\nhospital with undisclosed\nillness.\n13.12.16 treated by 38th\nCasualty Clearing Station\nthen to 14th\nAustralian Field\nAmbulance. 20.12.16\ntreated for myalgia at 10th\nGeneral Hospital Rouen,\nFrance. 8.1.17 evacuated to\nEngland on hospital ship St.\nDavid.\n12.1.17 admitted to 4th\nLondon General Hospital for\nneurasthenia (chronic\nfatigue).\n30.7.17 discharged from 1st\nAuxiliary Hospital,\nWeymouth with bilateral\nmuscular weakness.\n26.9.17 disembarked from\nhospital ship Pakaha at\nCapetown and admitted to\n2nd\nGeneral Hospital.\n29.3.18 granted a pension of\nthree pound per fortnight.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Private Warren\nfrom Dean had been a\nDistrict Volunteer.",
