    "service": "Joined 28.8.16. Service\nnumber: 2415. Rank: Private.\nRoll title: 38th\nInfantry\nBattalion, 1st\nto 6th\nReinforcements, (June to\nDecember 1916). Age on\nenlistment: 18 years 8\nmonths. Occupation:\nLabourer. Marital status:\nSingle. Religion: Church of\nEngland. Next of kin and\naddress: Father, John White,\nAllendale. Embarked Melbourne\n20.10.16 on ship A17 HMAT\nPort Lincoln. Rate of pay per\ndiem before and after\nembarkation: Five Shillings.\nOriginal unit: 38th\nBattalion,\n4th\nReinforcement.\nAustralian War Memorial\nEmbarkation Roll Number:\n23/55/2.\nLater in this publication are more\ndetails about the ships that took\nindividuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Allendale 1898. Birth\nRegistration 1898/85. Father: John\nWhite. Mother: Margaret\nJane Croy. Married Jean\nGlover 1924. Marriage Registration\n1924/731.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 28.8.16. Service\nnumber: 2415. Rank: Private.\nRoll title: 38th\nInfantry\nBattalion, 1st\nto 6th\nReinforcements, (June to\nDecember 1916). Age on\nenlistment: 18 years 8\nmonths. Occupation:\nLabourer. Marital status:\nSingle. Religion: Church of\nEngland. Next of kin and\naddress: Father, John White,\nAllendale.",
