    "service": "Joined 8.11.17 Ballarat.\nService number: 3596. Rank:\nPrivate. Roll title: 46th\nInfantry Battalion, 10th\nReinforcements, (February\n1918). Age on enlistment: 21\nyears 2 months. Occupation:\nBlacksmith (Ballarat).\nAddress at date of\nenlistment: Broomfield.\nMarital status: Single.\nReligion: Presbyterian. Next\nof kin and address: father, J.\nWilliams, Ararat. Embarked Melbourne\n28.2.18 on ship A71 HMAT\nNestor. Rate of pay per diem\nbefore embarkation: Six\nShillings. Original unit: 46th\nInfantry Battalion, 10th\nReinforcements.\nLater in this publication are more\ndetails about the ships that took\nindividuals overseas.",
    "family": "Born Broomfield 12.9.1896.\nBirth Registration 1896/25886.\nFather: John Williams.\nMother: Susan Green.\nMarried Rita Lillian James\n1924. Marriage Registration\n1924/2048.",
    "enlistment": "Joined 8.11.17 Ballarat.\nService number: 3596. Rank:\nPrivate. Roll title: 46th\nInfantry Battalion, 10th\nReinforcements, (February\n1918). Age on enlistment: 21\nyears 2 months. Occupation:\nBlacksmith (Ballarat).\nAddress at date of\nenlistment: Broomfield.\nMarital status: Single.\nReligion: Presbyterian. Next\nof kin and address: father, J.\nWilliams, Ararat.",
    "embarkation": "Embarked Melbourne\n28.2.18 on ship A71 HMAT\nNestor. Rate of pay per diem\nbefore embarkation: Six\nShillings. Original unit: 46th\nInfantry Battalion, 10th\nReinforcements.\nLater in this publication are more\ndetails about the ships that took\nindividuals overseas.",
    "fate": "1.7.19 returned to Australia\non the ship HT Frankfurt.\n26.9.19 discharged 3rd\nMilitary District.\nDied 1987. Death Registration\n1987/16224. Age at death, 91\nyears. Place of burial:\nCreswick Cemetery, where\nhe was recorded as a\nresident of Creswick.",
    "recognition": "• British War Medal.\n• Victory Medal.\n• Hollinwood State School\nHonour Board.\n• Kooroocheang State\nSchool Honour Board.\n• Broomfield State School\nHonour Board.\n• RSL Virtual War\nMemorial.\nAvenue of Honour Tree W106",
