    "additionalNotes": "7.7.17 an article from The\nBallarat Star reports that he\nwas wounded in action,\nnoting that he was Secretary\nof the local Fire Brigade prior\nto the war, and in the\nemploy of Mr. J. H. Wishart.\nThe article concludes: “His\nnumerous friends hope for a\nspeedy recovery.”",
    "notes": "Prior experience: Lieutenant\nin Senior Cadets, and six\nmonths with Citizen Forces.\n18.7.16 arrived Devonport,\nEngland.\n23.11.16 proceeded\noverseas to France via\nSouthampton.\n2.12.16 treated by 2nd\nAustralian Casualty Clearing\nStation before being\nadmitted to hospital with\nbronchitis. 14.12.16 rejoined\nBattalion.\n7.6.17 Wounded in Action.\n(Gassed.) Initially treated by\n9th\nAustralian Field\nAmbulance. Admitted to 7th\nCanadian General Hospital in\nEtaples, France. Rejoined\nBattalion in France on\n8.11.17.\n13.9.18 admitted to hospital\nwith undisclosed illness.\n20.9.18 evacuated to\nEngland. 21.9.18 at Reading\nMilitary Hospital, England,\nclassified as unfit for further\nmilitary service due to\ngassing.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Private\nWilliams from Broomfield\nhad been a District\nVolunteer.\n31.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported all from the\nBorough and Shire who had\nbeen Wounded in Action\nduring WW1 and that\nincluded Private Williams.",
