    "familyConnection": "",
    "additionalNotes": "At enlistment, he recorded\nhis birth at Powlett Hill, but\nthe birth was registered at\nSmeaton.\nOn his death registration,\nmother's maiden name was\nrecorded as unknown.",
    "notes": "16.10.17 based at\nBroadmeadows Camp with\n8th\nBattalion, M Company.\n16.10.17 he received the first\nof his three vaccinations.\n21.3.18 Medical History\nreport indicated that he had\nnot served overseas and that\nhe had suffered from pain in\nthe 4th\nmetatarsal for at least\n7 years. Pain has increased\nfor all the walking conducted\nduring training. Medical\nBoard opinion was that the\nproblem was chronic and\nthat he should be discharged\nimmediately.\n3.12.18 Creswick Advertiser\nreported that Private Wood\nfrom Powlett Hill had been a\nDistrict Volunteer.\n21.12.20 Army Base records\nMelbourne wrote to\nReturned Soldiers'\nQualification Committee to\nindicate that “Circumstances\nnot within his control\nrendered him unable to\nleave Australia for service\nabroad”.",
